:Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "BioSystem" ;
    rdfs:comment "Initialize a System for a Biological analysis.\nRetrieve, from the initial file, the basic fragments, the system sequence,\ntheir mutual interactions and the informations about the purity and the\nobservables\n\nArgs:\n   filename (str): a pdb file with fragment information inside\n   sys (System): an initial system, useful for a custom refragmentation.\n        If present, overrides the association written in the pdbfile.\n        It is user's responsibility to ensure coherency of the total\n        number of atoms.\n    sequence_from_fragments (bool): method to determine the sequences.\n        If True, the sequence are determined by the fragment names.\n        It is user's responsibility to provide a inputfile that has a\n        set of residues compatible with the fragmentation.\n    disable_warnings (bool): disable the BioPython warnings if true\n    structure (Bio.Structure): a system structure that is meant to replace\n        the one genrated by the file parser. Useful for corrupted pdb\n        files. To be used with `sequence from_fragments`\n    **kwargs: other arguments to be passed to `py:func:~BigDFT.IO.read_pdb`\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: atomic_bond_orders, atomic_frag_indices, atomic_interactions, bigdft_tool, bond_orders, calculate_contact_regions, calculate_target_interactions, charge_at_pH, chessboards, colordict, d3, d3PBE_energy, dispersion_interactions, display, display_graph, display_sequences, extract_target_contact_and_counter_region, frag_indices, fragment_distances, fragment_ids, fragment_interaction_and_feedback, fragment_interaction_strengths, fragment_purities, fragment_scatterplot, fragment_values, from_sys, identify_contact_region, interactions, ks_matrix, labeldict, override_fragment_association, purities, refragment, refragmentation_colordict, represent, set_archive_name, set_fragment_quantities, set_qm_run, sinvh_matrix, system_target_interaction_investigation, unmatched_frag_info.\nInherited: ase_potential_energy (from System), compute_matching (from System), dataframe_slicing (from System), dict (from System), distances_from_target (from System), examine (from System), get_external_potential (from System), get_k_nearest_fragments (from System), get_nearest_fragment (from System), get_net_force (from System), get_posinp (from System), reform_superunits (from System), rename_fragments (from System), serialize (from System), set_atom_forces (from System), set_atom_multipoles (from System), set_electrons_from_log (from System), set_logfile_info (from System), subsystem (from System), to_dataframe (from System), update_positions_from_dict (from System)." ;
    :hasDescription "Initialize a System for a Biological analysis. Retrieve, from the initial file, the basic fragments, the system sequence, their mutual interactions and the informations about the purity and the observables" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_BioQM ;
    :hasSignature "BioSystem(filename, sys=None, structure=None, sequence_from_fragments=False, disable_warnings=False, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "filename (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "sys=None" ;
    :hasArgument "structure=None" ;
    :hasArgument "sequence_from_fragments=False" ;
    :hasArgument "disable_warnings=False" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Systems_System .

:Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystemPopulation a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "BioSystemPopulation" ;
    rdfs:comment "An ensemble of BioSystem. Useful to provide and analyze averaged quantities\n\nArgs:\n   systems(dict, list): BioSystems defining the populations.\n       They can be provided as a dict of pdb files plus logfiles,\n       or as a dictionary of systems,\n       or as a dictionary of archives for serialization.\n       The dictionary is composed as follows:\n       'label': {'archive': <archive_filename>,\n                 'system': <BioSystem instance>,\n                 'filename': <pdbfile>,\n                 'logfile': <logfile_path>,\n                 'weight': weigth of the sample in the population,\n                 'mapping': provides the expression of the fragment of\n                     the representative in term of the fragments of the\n                     item of the population}\n        alternatively, a list can be employed, in which case the filling of\n        the population is performed sequentially\n   representative (str, int): label of the system representative of\n       the population\n   exclude_representative (bool): if True, the data of the population will\n       be evaluated without considering the representative\n   fragment_values (list): list of the internal fragment values that can\n       be found inside each of the system. Can be left as an empty list\n       to delegate all the evaluation to the populations.\n   fragment_interactions (list): list of the attributes which correspond\n       to the quantities which are associated to inter-fragment\n       interactions.\n   to_evaluate(dict) : dictionary of functions to be employed to\n       evaluate at the creation of a population.\n       They must provide a quantity that is related to a system.\n   chessboard_cutoffs (list): list of the cutoffs that will have\n       to be employed for the fragmentation.\n       Use an empty list to deactivate.\n   initial_view (dict): view of the superunits fragmentation that will be\n       employed to the representative in the lowest cutoff\n   **kwargs: arguments to be passed at the loading of the system\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: bond_orders, colordict, electrostatic_interactions, examine, fragment_scatterplot, fragment_values, interactions, load, purities, serialize.\nInherited: ase_potential_energy (from System), calculate_contact_regions (from BioSystem), calculate_target_interactions (from BioSystem), charge_at_pH (from BioSystem), chessboards (from BioSystem), compute_matching (from System), d3 (from BioSystem), d3PBE_energy (from BioSystem), dataframe_slicing (from System), dict (from System), dispersion_interactions (from BioSystem), display (from BioSystem), display_graph (from BioSystem), display_sequences (from BioSystem), distances_from_target (from System), extract_target_contact_and_counter_region (from BioSystem), fragment_distances (from BioSystem), fragment_interaction_and_feedback (from BioSystem), fragment_interaction_strengths (from BioSystem), get_external_potential (from System), get_k_nearest_fragments (from System), get_nearest_fragment (from System), get_net_force (from System), get_posinp (from System), identify_contact_region (from BioSystem), labeldict (from BioSystem), override_fragment_association (from BioSystem), reform_superunits (from System), refragment (from BioSystem), refragmentation_colordict (from BioSystem), rename_fragments (from System), represent (from BioSystem), set_archive_name (from BioSystem), set_atom_forces (from System), set_atom_multipoles (from System), set_electrons_from_log (from System), set_fragment_quantities (from BioSystem), set_logfile_info (from System), set_qm_run (from BioSystem), subsystem (from System), system_target_interaction_investigation (from BioSystem), to_dataframe (from System), unmatched_frag_info (from BioSystem), update_positions_from_dict (from System)." ;
    :hasDescription "An ensemble of BioSystem. Useful to provide and analyze averaged quantities" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_BioQM ;
    :hasSignature "BioSystemPopulation(systems, representative, fragment_values=['charge', 'dipole', 'purity'], to_evaluate=None, exclude_representative=False, chessboard_cutoffs=[0.05, 0.045, 0.04, 0.035, 0.03, 0.025], initial_view=None, fragment_interactions=['bond_orders', 'interactions', 'electrostatic_interactions'], **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "systems (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "representative (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "fragment_values=['charge', 'dipole', 'purity']" ;
    :hasArgument "to_evaluate=None" ;
    :hasArgument "exclude_representative=False" ;
    :hasArgument "chessboard_cutoffs=[0.05, 0.045, 0.04, 0.035, 0.03, 0.025]" ;
    :hasArgument "initial_view=None" ;
    :hasArgument "fragment_interactions=['bond_orders', 'interactions', 'electrostatic_interactions']" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem .

