:Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Dataset" ;
    rdfs:comment "A set of calculations.\n\nSuch class contains the various instances of a set of calculations with the\ncode.\nThe different calculations are labelled by parameter values and information\nthat might then be retrieved for inspection and plotting.\n\nArgs:\n  label (str): The label of the dataset. It will be needed to identify the\n      instance for example in plot titles or in the running directory.\n  run_dir (str): path of the directory where the runs will be performed.\n  input (dict): Inputfile to be used for the runs as default,\n         can be overridden by the specific inputs of the run\n\nConstructor: Set the dataset ready for appending new runs\n\nMethods and properties: append_run, fetch_results, get_logfiles, get_times, post_processing, process_run, seek_convergence, set_postprocessing_function, wait.\nInherited: get_global_option (from Runner), global_options (from Runner), pop_global_option (from Runner), pre_processing (from Runner), run (from Runner), update_global_options (from Runner)." ;
    :hasDescription "A set of calculations." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Datasets ;
    :hasSignature "Dataset(label='BigDFT dataset', run_dir='runs', **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "label='BigDFT dataset'" ;
    :hasArgument "run_dir='runs'" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0a567087a54d> .

:Class_BigDFT_DoS_DiracSuperposition a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "DiracSuperposition" ;
    rdfs:comment "Sum of weighted Dirac deltas.\n\nDefines a superposition of Dirac deltas which can be used to\nplot the density of states. Such deltas are given on a per k-point\nbasis and can be also equipped with a array of weights, which may be\nuseful to define Partial Density of States.\n\nArgs:\n   dos (matrix): array containing the density of states per each k-point.\n        Should be of shape 2, a list of energies per kpoint\n   wgts(float, array, matrix): contains the weights of each of the\n        k-points. Could be a constant, in which case the same weight is\n        applied everywhere, a list (on a k-point basis),\n        or a matrix, where each energy have its own weight.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: curve, peak, peaks." ;
    :hasDescription "Sum of weighted Dirac deltas." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_DoS ;
    :hasSignature "DiracSuperposition(dos, wgts=[1.0])" ;
    :hasArgument "dos (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "wgts=[1.0]" .

:Class_BigDFT_DoS_DoS a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "DoS" ;
    rdfs:comment "Density of states class.\n\nExtract a quantity which is associated to the DoS, that can be plotted\n\nArgs:\n    bandarrays (list): a list of :py:class:`~BigDFT.BZ.BandArray`\n        class instances.\n    energies (array-like): a list of energies to be plotted.\n        Useful for plotting a single DoS from an array.\n    evals (dict): dictionary of eigenvalues from a logfile yaml\n        serialization. May be useful if a\n        :py:class:`~BigDFT.Logfiles.Logfile` class is not available.\n    logfiles_dict(dict): dictionary of :py:class:`~BigDFT.Logfiles.Logfile`\n        class instances as values to be employed to create\n        the set of DoS. The keys of the dictionary are the labels of the\n        corresponding curves.\n    reference_fermi_level (float): useful in the case of a logfiles_dict.\n        the value of the reference fermi level is compared with the\n        fermi level of all the logfiles in order to align all the curves.\n        It is assumed that the fermi levels are properly defined in all\n        the logfiles.\n    units (str): The units of the provided energies, and fermi_level.\n        Should be `AU` of `eV`.\n    label (str): label of the curve.\n    sigma (float): smearing of the energies. Always provided in eV.\n    fermi_level(float): set the value of the fermi energy.\n    norm (float, list): weights of the :py:class:`DiracSuperposition`\n       instantation for each of the k-points.\n    sdos : spatial density of states instantiation\n    **kwargs: keyword arguments of the :py:meth:`set_range` method.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: append, append_from_bandarray, append_from_dict, dump, fermi_level, get_curves, plot, set_range, shift_curves, update." ;
    :hasDescription "Density of states class." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_DoS ;
    :hasSignature "DoS(bandarrays=None, energies=None, evals=None, logfiles_dict=None, units='eV', reference_fermi_level=None, label='1', sigma=0.2, fermi_level=None, norm=1.0, sdos=None, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "bandarrays=None" ;
    :hasArgument "energies=None" ;
    :hasArgument "evals=None" ;
    :hasArgument "logfiles_dict=None" ;
    :hasArgument "units='eV'" ;
    :hasArgument "reference_fermi_level=None" ;
    :hasArgument "label='1'" ;
    :hasArgument "sigma=0.2" ;
    :hasArgument "fermi_level=None" ;
    :hasArgument "norm=1.0" ;
    :hasArgument "sdos=None" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_Fragments_Fragment a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Fragment" ;
    rdfs:comment "A fragment is a list of atoms in a system. Fragment might have quantities\nassociated to it, like its electrostatic multipoles (charge, dipole, etc.)\nand also geometrical information (center of mass, principla axis etc.). A\nFragment might also be rototranslated and combined with other moieteies to\nform a :class:`BigDFT.Systems.Systems`.\n\nArgs:\n  atomlist (list): list of atomic dictionaries defining the fragment\n  xyzfile (BigDFT.IO.XYZReader): an XYZ file to read from.\n  posinp (dict): the posinp style dictionary from a logfile/input file.\n  astruct (dict): a BigDFT atomic structure style dictionary.\n  system (BigDFT.Systems.System): a BigDFT system, esssentially this\n    reduces many fragments into a single fragment.\n\n.. todo::\n   Define and describe if this API is also suitable for solid-state\n   fragments\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: center_of_charge, centroid, d0, d1, ellipsoid, get_external_potential, get_net_force, insert, nel, q0, qcharge, rmsd, rotate, rotate_on_axis, serialize, translate." ;
    :hasDescription "A fragment is a list of atoms in a system. Fragment might have quantities associated to it, like its electrostatic multipoles (charge, dipole, etc.) and also geometrical information (center of mass, principla axis etc.). A Fragment might also be rototranslated and combined with other moieteies to form a :class:`BigDFT.Systems.Systems`." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Fragments ;
    :hasSignature "Fragment(atomlist=None, xyzfile=None, posinp=None, astruct=None, system=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "atomlist=None" ;
    :hasArgument "xyzfile=None" ;
    :hasArgument "posinp=None" ;
    :hasArgument "astruct=None" ;
    :hasArgument "system=None" ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_76397a6ec4c2> .

:Class_BigDFT_Fragments_Rotation a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Rotation" ;
    rdfs:comment "This class defines a simple rotation.\n\nArgs:\n  t (list): the vector describing the rotation.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\nInherited: dot (from RotoTranslation), invert (from RotoTranslation)." ;
    :hasDescription "This class defines a simple rotation." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Fragments ;
    :hasSignature "Rotation(R)" ;
    :hasArgument "R (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Fragments_RotoTranslation .

:Class_BigDFT_Fragments_RotoTranslation a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RotoTranslation" ;
    rdfs:comment "Define a transformation which can be applied to a fragment. This\nrotation is defined by giving this class two fragments, and the\nrototranslation between those fragments is automatically computed.\n\nArgs:\n  frag1 (BigDFT.Fragments.Fragment): the first position.\n  frag2 (BigDFT.Fragments.Fragment): the second position.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: dot, invert." ;
    :hasDescription "Define a transformation which can be applied to a fragment. This rotation is defined by giving this class two fragments, and the rototranslation between those fragments is automatically computed." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Fragments ;
    :hasSignature "RotoTranslation(frag1, frag2)" ;
    :hasArgument "frag1 (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "frag2 (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_Fragments_Translation a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Translation" ;
    rdfs:comment "This class defines a simple translation.\n\nArgs:\n  t (list): the vector describing the translation.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\nInherited: dot (from RotoTranslation), invert (from RotoTranslation)." ;
    :hasDescription "This class defines a simple translation." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Fragments ;
    :hasSignature "Translation(t)" ;
    :hasArgument "t (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Fragments_RotoTranslation .

:Class_BigDFT_IO_XYZReader a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "XYZReader" ;
    rdfs:comment "A class which can be used to read from xyz files.\n\nThis class should behave like a standard file, which means you can use\nit in ``with`` statements, and use the ``next`` command to iterate over it.\n\nAttributes:\n  closed (bool): check if a file is open or not.\n  units (str): the units that the xyz file was in.\n  natoms (int): the number of atoms in the xyz file.\n  cell (list): a list of floats describing the cell.\n\nArgs:\n  filename (str): the file to read from. You can also specify a molecule\n    that might be in the database.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: close, closed, next, open." ;
    :hasDescription "A class which can be used to read from xyz files." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_IO ;
    :hasSignature "XYZReader(filename)" ;
    :hasArgument "filename (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_IO_XYZWriter a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "XYZWriter" ;
    rdfs:comment "A class for writing XYZ files.\n\nThis class should behave like a standard file, which means you can use\nit in ``with`` statements and write.\n\nArgs:\n  filename (str): the file to write to.\n  natoms (int): how many atoms we will write.\n  units (str): the units of the file. Defaults to angstroem.\n  cell (BigDFT.UnitCells.UnitCell): the unit cell.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: close, closed, open, write." ;
    :hasDescription "A class for writing XYZ files." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_IO ;
    :hasSignature "XYZWriter(filename, natoms, units='angstroem', cell=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "filename (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "natoms (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "units='angstroem'" ;
    :hasArgument "cell=None" .

:Class_BigDFT_Inputfiles_Inputfile a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Inputfile" ;
    rdfs:comment "The BigDFT inputfile.\n\nPrincipal object needed to run a  BigDFT calculation.\nMight be initialized either from a dictionary, a\n:py:class:`~BigDFT.Logfiles.Logfile` instance\nor a (yaml-compliant) filename path\n\nNote:\n\n   Each of the actions of the module :py:mod:`~BigDFT.InputActions`, which\n   is defined on a generic dictionary, also corresponds to a method of of\n   the `Inputfile` class, and it is applied to the class instance.\n   Therefore also the first argument of the corresponding action is\n   implicitly the class instance. For the\n   :py:func:`~BigDFT.InputActions.remove` method, the action has to be\n   invoked should come from the :py:mod:`~BigDFT.InputActions` module.\n\n\n.. _input_action_example:\nExample:\n\n   >>> import InputActions as A, Inputfiles as I\n   >>> inp=I.Inputfile()\n   >>> inp.set_hgrids(0.3) # equivalent to A.set_hgrids(inp,0.3)\n   >>> inp\n   {'dft': {'hgrids': 0.3}}\n   >>> inp.optimize_geometry() # equivalent to A.optimize_geometry(inp)\n   >>> inp\n   {'dft': {'hgrids': 0.3},'geopt': {'method': 'FIRE',\n                                     'ncount_cluster_x': 50} }\n   >>> # equivalent to A.remove(inp,A.optimize_geometry)\n   >>> inp.remove(A.optimize_geometry)\n   >>> inp\n   {'dft': {'hgrids': 0.3}}\n\n .. todo ::\n\n     Consider the possiblity of initializing an `Inputfile` instance\n     from a ``yaml`` file. And also from a\n     :py:class:`~BigDFT.Logfiles.Logfile` class\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature." ;
    :hasDescription "The BigDFT inputfile." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Inputfiles ;
