:Class_BigDFT_Interop_XTBInterop_XTBCalculator a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "XTBCalculator" ;
    rdfs:comment "A calculator which can drive simulations using the XTB program.\n\nXTB uses a mixed approach for control. First, you can pass command line\narguments to the program. Second, you can modify the input file. We\nmirror this split here. Command line arguments can be passed as arguments\nto the run command. To modify the input file, the run command accepts\nan argument `inp` which is a dictionary. This dictionary is written\nto the input file (in the appropriate format). See the example for\nmore details.\n\nhttps://xtb-docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/contents.html\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: post_processing, pre_processing, process_run.\nInherited: get_global_option (from Runner), global_options (from Runner), pop_global_option (from Runner), run (from Runner), update_global_options (from Runner)." ;
    :hasDescription "A calculator which can drive simulations using the XTB program." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Interop_XTBInterop ;
    :hasSignature "XTBCalculator(omp='4', dry_run=False, skip=False, verbose=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "omp='4'" ;
    :hasArgument "dry_run=False" ;
    :hasArgument "skip=False" ;
    :hasArgument "verbose=True" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner .

:Class_BigDFT_Interop_XTBInterop_XTBLogfile a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "XTBLogfile" ;
    rdfs:comment "This class stores the results of an XTB calculation which might be later\npost-processed.\n\nAttributes:\n    sys (BigDFT.Systems.System): a handle to the original system used\n        in the calculation.\n    log (str): a string representation of the logfile from XTB.\n    charges (list): charge values computed by XTB.\n    opt_energy (list): a list of energy values from the geometry\n        optimization procedure.\n    opt_fnorm (list): a list of gradient norm values from the geometry\n        optimization procedure.\n    opt_traj (list): a list of BigDFT.Systems.System from the geometry\n        optimization procedure.\n    md_energy (list): a list of energy values from the MD simulation.\n    md_fnorm (list): a list of gradient norm values from the MD simulation.\n    md_traj (list): a list of BigDFT.Systems.System from the MD simulation.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: energy, gfnff_qest, gradient_norm, homo_lumo_gap." ;
    :hasDescription "This class stores the results of an XTB calculation which might be later post-processed." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Interop_XTBInterop ;
    :hasSignature "XTBLogfile(sys, logname, opt=False, md=False)" ;
    :hasArgument "sys (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "logname (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "opt=False" ;
    :hasArgument "md=False" .

:Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_CouplingMatrix a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "CouplingMatrix" ;
    rdfs:comment "Casida Coupling Matrix, extracted from the calculation performed by BigDFT\n\nMethods and properties: diagonalize, subportion." ;
    :hasDescription "Casida Coupling Matrix, extracted from the calculation performed by BigDFT" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_LRTDDFT ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionMatrix .

:Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_Excitations a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Excitations" ;
    rdfs:comment "LR Excited states of a system\n\nDefinition of the excited states in the Casida Formalism\n\nArgs:\n   cm (CouplingMatrix): the matrix of coupling among transitions\n   tm (TransitionMultipoles): scalar product of multipoles among\n     transitions\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: determine_occ_energies, dos, dos_dict, identify_singlet_and_triplets, identify_thresholds, lookup, plot_Sminustwo, plot_alpha, plot_excitation_landscape, project_on_spin, spectrum_curves, split_excitations." ;
    :hasDescription "LR Excited states of a system" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_LRTDDFT ;
    :hasSignature "Excitations(cm, tm)" ;
    :hasArgument "cm (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "tm (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionDipoles a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "TransitionDipoles" ;
    rdfs:comment "Transition dipoles as provided in the version of the code < 1.8.0.\nDeprecated, to be used in some particular cases\n\nMethods and properties: get_transitions.\nInherited: subportion (from TransitionMultipoles)." ;
    :hasDescription "Transition dipoles as provided in the version of the code < 1.8.0. Deprecated, to be used in some particular cases" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_LRTDDFT ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionMultipoles .

:Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionMatrix a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "TransitionMatrix" ;
    rdfs:comment "Matrix of Transition Quantities, might be either :class:`CouplingMatrix`\nor :class:`TransitionMultipoles`\n\nArgs:\n    matrix (matrix-like): data of the coupling matrix. If present also\n      the number of orbitals should be provided.\n    norb_occ (tuple): number of occupied orbitals per spin channnel.\n      Compulsory if ``matrix`` is specified.\n    norb_virt (tuple): number of empty orbitals per spin channnel.\n      Compulsory if ``matrix`` is specified.\n    log (Logfile): Instance of the logfile from which the coupling matrix\n      calculation is performed. Automatically retrieves the ``norb_occ``\n      and `norb_virt`` parameters. When ``log`` parameter is present the\n      parameter ``matrix`` is ignored.\n\nRaises:\n    ValueError: if the file of the coupling matrix indicated by ``log``\n      does not exists\n\nConstructor: Perform sanity checks on the loaded matrix" ;
    :hasDescription "Matrix of Transition Quantities, might be either :class:`CouplingMatrix` or :class:`TransitionMultipoles`" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_LRTDDFT ;
    :hasSignature "TransitionMatrix(*args, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "args (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionMultipoles a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "TransitionMultipoles" ;
    rdfs:comment "Transition dipoles, extracted from the calculation performed by BigDFT\n\nMethods and properties: get_transitions, subportion." ;
    :hasDescription "Transition dipoles, extracted from the calculation performed by BigDFT" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_LRTDDFT ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_LRTDDFT_TransitionMatrix .

:Class_BigDFT_Logfiles_Energies a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Energies" ;
    rdfs:comment "Find the energy terms from a BigDFT logfile.\nMay also accept malformed logfiles that are issued, for instance,\nfrom a badly terminated run that had I/O error.\n\nArgs:\n    filename (str): path of the logfile\n    units (str): may be 'AU' or 'kcal/mol'\n    disp (float): dispersion energy (will be added to the total energy)\n    strict (bool): assume a well-behaved logfile\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: to_dict." ;
    :hasDescription "Find the energy terms from a BigDFT logfile. May also accept malformed logfiles that are issued, for instance, from a badly terminated run that had I/O error." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Logfiles ;
    :hasSignature "Energies(filename, units='AU', disp=None, strict=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "filename (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "units='AU'" ;
    :hasArgument "disp=None" ;
    :hasArgument "strict=True" .

:Class_BigDFT_Logfiles_Logfile a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "Logfile" ;
    rdfs:comment "Import a Logfile from a filename in yaml format, a list of filenames,\nan archive (compressed tar file), a dictionary or a list of dictionaries.\n\nArgs:\n    *args: sequence of logfiles to be parsed. If it is longer than\n        one item, the logfiles are considered as belonging to the same run.\n    **kwargs: describes how the data can be read. Keywords can be:\n\n       * archive: name of the archive from which retrieve the logfiles.\n\n       * member: name of the logfile within the archive. If absent, all the\n           files of the archive will be considered as args.\n\n       * label: the label of the logfile instance\n\n       * dictionary: parsed logfile given as a dictionary,\n           serialization of the yaml logfile\n\nExample:\n   >>> l = Logfile('one.yaml','two.yaml')\n   >>> l = Logfile(archive='calc.tgz')\n   >>> l = Logfile(archive='calc.tgz',member='one.yaml')\n   >>> l = Logfile(dictionary=dict1)\n   >>> l = Logfile(dictionary=[dict1, dict2])\n\nTodo:\n   Document the automatically generated attributes, perhaps via an inner\n   function in futile python module\n\nConstructor: Initialize the class\n\nMethods and properties: geopt_plot, get_brillouin_zone, get_dos, wfn_plot." ;
    :hasDescription "Import a Logfile from a filename in yaml format, a list of filenames, an archive (compressed tar file), a dictionary or a list of dictionaries." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_Logfiles ;
    :hasSignature "Logfile(*args, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "args (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_16dc4c2b2af1> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_24a1fde40aa8> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_3edc0e7b8be5> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_47fc2d353eb4> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_494dcb5bb347> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_5fb8fd409fbe> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_90e6dfaaa9a3> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_a330b04a1611> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_ab6f691cfd10> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_b8ba0bca0fcb> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_bc671d09a148> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_e8020e9c619c> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_eb9431b43940> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_f12ccdac8f92> ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_fef6feefdaa1> .

:Class_BigDFT_PointParticles_PointParticles a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "PointParticles" ;
    rdfs:comment "An object storing the point particle information\n\nArgs:\n    X (array): array of atomic positions\n    Q (array): charge monopoles of the electrons\n    Z (array): charge monopole of the ions\n    P (array): electrostatic dipoles\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: Eel, Eel_dict, Elr, Elr_dict, R, Rm1." ;
    :hasDescription "An object storing the point particle information" ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_PointParticles ;
    :hasSignature "PointParticles(X, Z=None, Q=None, P=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "X (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "Z=None" ;
    :hasArgument "Q=None" ;
    :hasArgument "P=None" .

:Class_BigDFT_PostProcessing_BigDFTool a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "BigDFTool" ;
    rdfs:comment "This module defines the actions that can be performed using the\n``bigdft-tool`` python script. Such a script sometimes invokes the\n``memguess`` executable, which is executed serially. Sometimes the\n``utilities`` main program is necessary to take care of more time\nconsuming operations which require parallelism. We might also use\nthe ``obabel`` wrapper provided by BigDFT.\n\nArgs:\n  omp (int): number of OpenMP threads.\n    It defaults to the $OMP_NUM_THREADS variable in the environment,\n    if present, otherwise it fixes the run to 1 thread.\n  mpi_run (str): define the MPI command to be used.\n    It defaults to the value $BIGDFT_MPIRUN of the environment, if present.\n    When using this calculator into a job submission script, the value of\n    $BIGDFT_MPIRUN variable may be set appropriately to launch the bigdft\n    executable.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: auto_fragment, ccs_node, compute_fragment_dos, create_layered_qmmm_system, create_qmmm_system, derived_quantity, fragment_bond_order, fragment_interaction_energy, fragment_mask_matrix, fragment_population, generate_link_atoms, get_frag_indices, get_ks_coeff, get_matrix_h, get_matrix_k, get_matrix_kxs, get_matrix_s, get_matrix_sinvh, run_compute_purity." ;
    :hasDescription "This module defines the actions that can be performed using the ``bigdft-tool`` python script. Such a script sometimes invokes the ``memguess`` executable, which is executed serially. Sometimes the ``utilities`` main program is necessary to take care of more time consuming operations which require parallelism. We might also use the ``obabel`` wrapper provided by BigDFT." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_PostProcessing ;
    :hasSignature "BigDFTool(omp=1, mpi_run=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "omp=1" ;
    :hasArgument "mpi_run=None" .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteDataset a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteDataset" ;
    rdfs:comment "Defines a set of remote runs, to be executed from a base script and to\na provided url. This class is associated to a set of remote submissions,\nwhich may contain multiple calculations. All those calculations are\nexpressed to a single url, with a single base script, but with a collection\nof multiple remote runners that may provide different arguments.\n\nArgs:\n    label (str): man label of the dataset.\n    run_dir (str): local directory of preparation of the data.\n    database_file (str): name of the database file to keep track of the\n        submitted runs.\n    force (str): force the execution of the dataset regardless of the\n        database status.\n    **kwargs: global arguments of the appended remote runners.\n\nConstructor: Set the dataset ready for appending new runs\n\nMethods and properties: append_run, pre_processing, process_run.\nInherited: fetch_results (from Dataset), get_global_option (from Runner), get_logfiles (from Dataset), get_times (from Dataset), global_options (from Runner), pop_global_option (from Runner), post_processing (from Dataset), run (from Runner), seek_convergence (from Dataset), set_postprocessing_function (from Dataset), update_global_options (from Runner), wait (from Dataset)." ;
    :hasDescription "Defines a set of remote runs, to be executed from a base script and to a provided url. This class is associated to a set of remote submissions, which may contain multiple calculations. All those calculations are expressed to a single url, with a single base script, but with a collection of multiple remote runners that may provide different arguments." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteDataset(label='RemoteDataset', run_dir='/tmp', database_file='database.yaml', force=False, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "label='RemoteDataset'" ;
    :hasArgument "run_dir='/tmp'" ;
    :hasArgument "database_file='database.yaml'" ;
    :hasArgument "force=False" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteDillFunction a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteDillFunction" ;
    rdfs:comment "Serialize and execute remotely a python function, serialized with dill.\n\nWith this class we serilize and execute a python function\non a remote filesystem. This filesystem may be a remote computer\nor a different directory of the local machine.\n\nSuch class is useful to be employed in runners which needs to be executed\noutside of the current framework, butfor which the result is needed to\ncontinue the processing of the data.\n\nArgs:\n    name (str): the name of the remote function\n    function (func): the python function to be serialized.\n        The return value of the function should be an object for which\n        a relatively light-weight serialization is possible.\n    submitter (str): the interpreter to be invoked. Should be, e.g.\n        `python` if the function is a python function, or `bash`.\n    required_files (list): list of extra files that may be required for\n        the good running of the function.\n    output_files (list): list of the files that the function will produce\n        that are supposed to be retrieved to the host computer.\n    **kwargs:  keyword arguments of the function.\n        The arguments of the function should be serializable without\n        the requirement of too much disk space.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: append_function.\nInherited: call (from RemoteFunction), fetch_result (from RemoteFunction), files_received (from RemoteFunction), files_sent (from RemoteFunction), is_finished (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_receive (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_send (from RemoteFunction), receive_files (from RemoteFunction), send_files (from RemoteFunction), send_to (from RemoteFunction), setup (from RemoteFunction)." ;
    :hasDescription "Serialize and execute remotely a python function, serialized with dill." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteDillFunction(submitter, name, function, required_files=[], output_files=[], **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "submitter (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "name (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "function (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "required_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "output_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteFunction .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteFunction a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteFunction" ;
    rdfs:comment "Serialize and execute remotely a python function.\n\nWith this class we serilize and execute a python function\non a remote filesystem. This filesystem may be a remote computer\nor a different directory of the local machine.\n\nSuch class is useful to be employed in runners which needs to be executed\noutside of the current framework, butfor which the result is needed to\ncontinue the processing of the data.\n\nArgs:\n    name (str): the name of the remote function\n    function (func): the python function to be serialized.\n        The return value of the function should be an object for which\n        a relatively light-weight serialization is possible.\n    submitter (str): the interpreter to be invoked. Should be, e.g.\n        `python` if the function is a python function, or `bash`.\n    **kwargs:  keyword arguments of the function.\n        The arguments of the function should be serializable without\n        the requirement of too much disk space.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: append_function, call, fetch_result, files_received, files_sent, is_finished, prepare_files_to_receive, prepare_files_to_send, receive_files, send_files, send_to, setup." ;
    :hasDescription "Serialize and execute remotely a python function." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteFunction(submitter, name, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "submitter (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "name (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteJSONFunction a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteJSONFunction" ;
    rdfs:comment "Serialize and execute remotely a python function, serialized with JSON.\n\nWith this class we serilize and execute a python function\non a remote filesystem. This filesystem may be a remote computer\nor a different directory of the local machine.\n\nSuch class is useful to be employed in runners which needs to be executed\noutside of the current framework, for which the result is needed locally to\ncontinue data processing.\n\nArgs:\n    name (str): the name of the remote function\n    function (func): the python function to be serialized.\n        The return value of the function should be an object for which\n        a relatively light-weight serialization is possible.\n    submitter (str): the interpreter to be invoked. Should be, e.g.\n        `python` if the function is a python function, or `bash`.\n    extra_encoder_functions (list)): list of dictionaries of the format\n        {'cls': Class, 'func': function} which is employed to serialize\n        non-instrinsic objects as well as non-numpy objects.\n    required_files (list): list of extra files that may be required for\n        the good running of the function.\n    output_files (list): list of the files that the function will produce\n        that are supposed to be retrieved to the host computer.\n    **kwargs:  keyword arguments of the function.\n        The arguments of the function should be serializable without\n        the requirement of too much disk space.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: append_function.\nInherited: call (from RemoteFunction), fetch_result (from RemoteFunction), files_received (from RemoteFunction), files_sent (from RemoteFunction), is_finished (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_receive (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_send (from RemoteFunction), receive_files (from RemoteFunction), send_files (from RemoteFunction), send_to (from RemoteFunction), setup (from RemoteFunction)." ;
    :hasDescription "Serialize and execute remotely a python function, serialized with JSON." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteJSONFunction(submitter, name, function, extra_encoder_functions=[], required_files=[], output_files=[], **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "submitter (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "name (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "function (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "extra_encoder_functions=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "required_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "output_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteFunction .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteRunner a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteRunner" ;
    rdfs:comment "This class can be used to run python functions on a remote machine. This\nclass combines the execution of a script with a python remote function.\n\nArgs:\n\n    function (func): the python function to be serialized.\n        The return value of the function should be an object for which\n        a relatively light-weight serialization is possible.\n    name (str): the name of the remote function. Function name is employed\n        if not provided.\n    script (str): The script to be executed provided in string form.\n        The result file of the script is assumed to be named\n        `<name>-script-result`.\n    submitter (str): the interpreter to be invoked. Should be, e.g.\n        `bash` if the script is a shell script, or `qsub` if this is a\n        submission script.\n    url (str): the url you would use to ssh into that remote machine.\n    remote_dir (str): the path to the work directory on the remote machine.\n       Should be associated to a writable directory.\n    skip (bool): if true, we perform a lazy calculation.\n    asynchronous (bool): If True, submit the calculation without waiting\n       for the results.\n    local_dir (str): local directory to prepare the IO files to send.\n        The directory should exist and write permission should\n        be granted.\n    python (str): python interpreter to be invoked in the script.\n    protocol (str): serialization method to be invoked for the function.\n        can be 'JSON' of 'Dill', depending of the desired version.\n    extra_encoder_functions (list)): list of dictionaries of the format\n        {'cls': Class, 'func': function} which is employed to serialize\n        non-instrinsic objects as well as non-numpy objects. Useful for\n        the 'JSON' protocol.\n    required_files (list): list of extra files that may be required for\n        the good running of the function.\n    output_files (list): list of the files that the function will produce\n        that are supposed to be retrieved to the host computer.\n    arguments (dict):  keyword arguments of the function.\n        The arguments of the function should be serializable without\n        the requirement of too much disk space. Such arguments cannot\n        be named in the same way as the others.\n    **kwargs (dict):  Further keyword arguments of the script,\n        which will be substituted in the string representation.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\n\nMethods and properties: post_processing, pre_processing, process_run.\nInherited: append_function (from RemoteFunction), call (from RemoteFunction), fetch_result (from RemoteFunction), files_received (from RemoteFunction), files_sent (from RemoteFunction), get_global_option (from Runner), global_options (from Runner), is_finished (from RemoteFunction), pop_global_option (from Runner), prepare_files_to_receive (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_send (from RemoteFunction), receive_files (from RemoteFunction), run (from Runner), send_files (from RemoteFunction), send_to (from RemoteFunction), setup (from RemoteFunction), update_global_options (from Runner)." ;
    :hasDescription "This class can be used to run python functions on a remote machine. This class combines the execution of a script with a python remote function." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteRunner(function, submitter='bash', name=None, url='localhost', skip=True, asynchronous=True, remote_dir='.', ssh='ssh', rsync='rsync -auv', local_dir='/tmp', script='#!/bin/bash\\n', python='python', arguments={}, protocol='JSON', extra_encoder_functions=[], required_files=[], output_files=[], **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "function (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "submitter='bash'" ;
    :hasArgument "name=None" ;
    :hasArgument "url='localhost'" ;
    :hasArgument "skip=True" ;
    :hasArgument "asynchronous=True" ;
    :hasArgument "remote_dir='.'" ;
    :hasArgument "ssh='ssh'" ;
    :hasArgument "rsync='rsync -auv'" ;
    :hasArgument "local_dir='/tmp'" ;
    :hasArgument "script='#!/bin/bash\\n'" ;
    :hasArgument "python='python'" ;
    :hasArgument "arguments={}" ;
    :hasArgument "protocol='JSON'" ;
    :hasArgument "extra_encoder_functions=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "required_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "output_files=[]" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteScript .

:Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteScript a :PythonClass ;
    rdfs:label "RemoteScript" ;
    rdfs:comment "Triggers the remote execution of a script.\n\nThis class is useful to execute remotely a script and to retrieve.\nThe results of such execution. It inherits from the `RemoteFunction`\nbase class and extends some of its actions to the concept of the script.\n\nArgs:\n    name (str): the name of the remote function\n    script (str, func): The script to be executed provided in string form.\n        It can also be provided as a function which returns a string.\n    result_file(str): the name of the file in which the script\n        should redirect.\n    submitter (str): the interpreter to be invoked. Should be, e.g.\n        `bash` if the script is a shell script, or 'qsub' if this is a\n        submission script.\n    output_files (list): list of the files that the function will produce\n        that are supposed to be retrieved to the host computer.\n    **kwargs:  keyword arguments of the script-script function,\n        which will be substituted in the string representation.\n\nConstructor: Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\nInherited: append_function (from RemoteFunction), call (from RemoteFunction), fetch_result (from RemoteFunction), files_received (from RemoteFunction), files_sent (from RemoteFunction), is_finished (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_receive (from RemoteFunction), prepare_files_to_send (from RemoteFunction), receive_files (from RemoteFunction), send_files (from RemoteFunction), send_to (from RemoteFunction), setup (from RemoteFunction)." ;
    :hasDescription "Triggers the remote execution of a script." ;
    :definedIn :Module_BigDFT_RemoteRunners ;
    :hasSignature "RemoteScript(submitter, name, script, result_file, output_files, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "submitter (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "name (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "script (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "result_file (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "output_files (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :inheritsFrom :Class_BigDFT_RemoteRunners_RemoteFunction .

