:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_calculate_contact_regions a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "calculate_contact_regions" ;
    rdfs:comment "Identify the contact with a target.\n\nSingle out the portion of the target fragments\nthat interacts with the rest of the system, and store it.\n\nArgs:\n    target (list): fragments of the target region.\n    cutoff_bo (float): the value of the Fragment Bond Order\n        above which the fragments are considered to be\n        interacting. Typical values range between 0.01 and 1.e-3.\n    cutoff_el (float): cutoff for the electrostatic value (kcal/mol).\n        Fragments whose interaction is larger than such value are also\n        included in the contact region.\n    name (str): Name of the region to be stored in the fragment_values." ;
    :hasDescription "Identify the contact with a target." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "calculate_contact_regions(target, cutoff_bo=0.001, cutoff_el=10000000000.0, name='')" ;
    :hasArgument "target (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "cutoff_bo=0.001" ;
    :hasArgument "cutoff_el=10000000000.0" ;
    :hasArgument "name=''" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_calculate_target_interactions a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "calculate_target_interactions" ;
    rdfs:comment "Calculate the interaction terms with a target.\n\nThis function stores the fragment quantities associated to the\ninteraction term with a target.\n\nArgs:\n    target (list): list of the fragments of the target region\n    name (str): Name of the region to be stored in the fragment values.\n    include_dispersion (bool): if true, calculate also the dispersion\n       interaction of the target with the environment.\n       The dispersion is only calculated in the contact fragments.\n       Therefore if this value it true it is assumeed that the\n       contact regions have already been calculated and stored.\n    nthreads (int): number of threads for the parallel evaluation\n       of the dispersion" ;
    :hasDescription "Calculate the interaction terms with a target." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "calculate_target_interactions(target, name='', include_dispersion=False, nthreads=1)" ;
    :hasArgument "target (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "name=''" ;
    :hasArgument "include_dispersion=False" ;
    :hasArgument "nthreads=1" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_charge_at_pH a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "charge_at_pH" ;
    rdfs:comment "Identify the charge that the system should have for a given pH.\nEmploy the\n`~py:meth:Bio.Bio.SeqUtils.ProtParam.ProteinAnalysis.charge_at_ph`\nmethod of BioPython\n\nArgs:\n    ph (float): the value of the ph\n    closed_shell (bool): defines if the charge should be rounded\n        to the nearest even integer considering the total number\n        of electrons of the system.\nReturns:\n    float : the value of the charge" ;
    :hasDescription "Identify the charge that the system should have for a given pH. Employ the `~py:meth:Bio.Bio.SeqUtils.ProtParam.ProteinAnalysis.charge_at_ph` method of BioPython" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "charge_at_pH(ph, closed_shell=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "ph (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "closed_shell=True" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_chessboards a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "chessboards" ;
    rdfs:comment "Define a coherent group of fragmentations that are provided\nfrom the loosest to tightest cutoffs.\nThe views of the fragmentations are defined such as the tighest\ncutoffs always contain regrouping of fragments from the loosest\n\nArgs:\n    cutoffs (list): list of floating point numbers of the desired\n        cutoffs values\n    initial_view (dict): mapping of the initial fragmentation that will\n        be imposed strating from the loosest cutoff\nReturns:\n    dict: dictionary of the view. the values of the dictionary are\n        length-1 lists such that subsequent views (for instance found\n        when instantiating a population) can be appended" ;
    :hasDescription "Define a coherent group of fragmentations that are provided from the loosest to tightest cutoffs. The views of the fragmentations are defined such as the tighest cutoffs always contain regrouping of fragments from the loosest" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "chessboards(cutoffs, initial_view=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "cutoffs (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "initial_view=None" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_colordict a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "colordict" ;
    rdfs:comment "Define the colordict to quantify the fragments\naccording to the method.\n\nArgs:\n   keys (list): keys of the fragment names.\n   color_by (str): can be 'charge', 'dipole', 'purity'.\n   field_vals(list) : values of the field to decide\n         the colors of the keys.\n   colordict (dict) :  the dictionary of the keys,\n         and the corresponding colors. Overrides field_vals if present\n   colorcode (str): the string of the colorcode. can be 'html' or 'rgb'\n        if field_dict is absent, otherwise it represents\n        the colormap of matplotlib.\n        Default is 'seismic' for diverging values\n        (i.e. field_dict has negative data), otherwise 'Reds'.\n    highlight (list) : color in red only the fragments which\n        are indicated in the list.\n    view (dict): the fragmentation of the system to aggregate\n        the field_vals to.\n    highlight_color (matplotlib.colors): color to be employed\n        for highlighting." ;
    :hasDescription "Define the colordict to quantify the fragments according to the method." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "colordict(color_by=None, keys=None, field_vals=None, colordict=None, colorcode='html', highlight=None, view=None, vmin=None, vmax=None, highlight_color='red')" ;
    :hasArgument "color_by=None" ;
    :hasArgument "keys=None" ;
    :hasArgument "field_vals=None" ;
    :hasArgument "colordict=None" ;
    :hasArgument "colorcode='html'" ;
    :hasArgument "highlight=None" ;
    :hasArgument "view=None" ;
    :hasArgument "vmin=None" ;
    :hasArgument "vmax=None" ;
    :hasArgument "highlight_color='red'" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_d3 a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "d3" ;
    :hasDescription "Method d3 of BioSystem (no docstring)." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "d3()" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_d3PBE_energy a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "d3PBE_energy" ;
    rdfs:comment "Full dispersion energy of the system, or of a subsystem.\n\nArgs:\n    subsystem (list): fragment to focus on. If absent, the\n        entire system is considered.\n    erase_d3_files (bool): If true remove the d3 files\n        once the calculation is completed.\n\nReturns:\n    float: the d3 PBE energy for the PBE functional, in Hartree." ;
    :hasDescription "Full dispersion energy of the system, or of a subsystem." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "d3PBE_energy(subsystem=None, erase_d3_files=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "subsystem=None" ;
    :hasArgument "erase_d3_files=True" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_dispersion_interactions a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "dispersion_interactions" ;
    rdfs:comment "Van der Waals interaction strengths.\n\nExtract the dictionary of the dispersion interactions\nBetween two disjoint regions.\n\nArgs:\n    region1 (list): list of fragments of region 1\n    region2 (list): list of fragments of region 2\n    nthreads (int): number of omp threads to perform the calculation." ;
    :hasDescription "Van der Waals interaction strengths." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "dispersion_interactions(region1, region2, nthreads=1)" ;
    :hasArgument "region1 (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "region2 (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "nthreads=1" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_display a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "display" ;
    :hasDescription "Display the system using the inline visualizer of Py3DMol" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "display(cartoon=False, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "cartoon=False" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_display_graph a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "display_graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "Display a graph view of the system.\n\nWith this routine the fragments of the system are represented\nas a Graph, connected by the Fragment Bond Order criteria.\nGraph nodes can be represented as with a color map that is provided\nin a similar way than the sequence display.\n\nArgs:\n   restrict_to (list): list of fragments to which the graph\n         has to be restricted.\n   bo_cutoff (float): the limit for a non-negligible chemical link\n   fragment_labels (list, dict): list (in fragment_names order) of the\n       labels of the fragments or dictionary of the fragments which\n       need relabelling.\n   fragment_shapes (dict): per-fragment dictionary of the shapes to be\n       employed in the graph drawing.\n       Only non-default values are indicated. If absent,\n       the nodes which belong to the `restrict_to` list will\n       be represented  as squares, and the others as circles.\n   edge_labels (dict): dictionary of dictionaries: labels to be\n       written next to the edges, with keys indicating the fragment\n       names.\n   ax (matplotlib.pyplot.axes): matplotlib axis\n   colorbar_label(str): label to be associated to the colorbar.\n       If None, no colorbar is drawn.\n   bond_orders (dict-like): dictionary of the bond orders.\n       Supersedes the systems' bond order if present.\n       Not compatible with a view.\n   edge_colordict_kw (dict): dictionary of the keyword arguments\n       of the edge colors. The same syntax of the `colordict` method\n       is allowed, written in terms of the tuple of the fragments.\n       An additional keyword argument, `colordict_special`, is also\n       allowed. This one overrides the arguments provided by the\n       colordict for the fragment tuples provided.\n   node_edge_colordict_kw (dict): dictionary of the keyword arguments\n       of the node border colors. The same syntax of the `colordict`\n       method is allowed.\n   display_kwargs (dict): dictionary of the keyword arguments to be\n       passed to `Graph.display` method.\n   **kwargs: colordict arguments.\n\nReturns:\n    matplotlib.pyplot.axes: the axes of the displayed graph" ;
    :hasDescription "Display a graph view of the system." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "display_graph(restrict_to=None, bo_cutoff=0.01, fragment_labels=None, fragment_shapes=None, ax=None, colorbar_label='', edge_labels=None, bond_orders=None, edge_colordict_kw=None, node_edge_colordict_kw=None, display_kwargs={}, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "restrict_to=None" ;
    :hasArgument "bo_cutoff=0.01" ;
    :hasArgument "fragment_labels=None" ;
    :hasArgument "fragment_shapes=None" ;
    :hasArgument "ax=None" ;
    :hasArgument "colorbar_label=''" ;
    :hasArgument "edge_labels=None" ;
    :hasArgument "bond_orders=None" ;
    :hasArgument "edge_colordict_kw=None" ;
    :hasArgument "node_edge_colordict_kw=None" ;
    :hasArgument "display_kwargs={}" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_display_sequences a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "display_sequences" ;
    rdfs:comment "Display the full sequencies of the system.\nEmploy the given field to define the color dict if available\n\nArgs:\n   field_vals(list) : values of the field to decide\n       the colors of the keys\n   labeldict (dict): an optional dictionary mapping fragment ids\n       to strings that will be printed on each sequence square.\n   colordict (dict) :  the dictionary of the keys,\n       and the corresponding colors. Overrides field_vals if present\n   axs (list): list of the axis in which to plot the sequences\n   with_fragment_labels (bool): a boolean useful to represent the\n       fragment numbers. Can be combined with a view to visualize the\n       QM fragments. Provides a default labeldict.\n   remove_letters (list): list of the letters to be removed from\n       the display. In elements of the chains.\n   **kwargs: arguments to be passed to display of the colordict\nReturns:\n   list: list of the axis of the sequences" ;
    :hasDescription "Display the full sequencies of the system. Employ the given field to define the color dict if available" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "display_sequences(axs=None, labeldict=None, boxcount=None, with_fragment_labels=False, remove_letters=None, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "axs=None" ;
    :hasArgument "labeldict=None" ;
    :hasArgument "boxcount=None" ;
    :hasArgument "with_fragment_labels=False" ;
    :hasArgument "remove_letters=None" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem_extract_target_contact_and_counter_region a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "extract_target_contact_and_counter_region" ;
    rdfs:comment "Extract the contact region in the target and counter-region.\n\nArgs:\n    name (str): name of the stored region to extract" ;
    :hasDescription "Extract the contact region in the target and counter-region." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_BioQM_BioSystem ;
    :hasSignature "extract_target_contact_and_counter_region(name='')" ;
    :hasArgument "name=''" .

