:Function_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator_post_processing a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "post_processing" ;
    rdfs:comment "Check the existence and the log file and return an instance logfile.\n\nReturns:\n       (Logfile) Instance of the logfile associated to the run.\n       associated to the run which has been just performed.\n       If the run failed for some reasons, the logfile seem not\n       existing or it cannot be parsed it returns `None`.\n\nRaises:\n       ValueError: if the logfile does not exists or is not accessible\n\nTodo:\n   Set the return value of run in the case of a run_file. It should be\n   a list of Logfile classes" ;
    :hasDescription "Check the existence and the log file and return an instance logfile." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :hasSignature "post_processing(timedbg, logname, command)" ;
    :hasArgument "timedbg (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "logname (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "command (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator_pre_processing a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "pre_processing" ;
    rdfs:comment "Process local run dictionary to create the input directory and identify\nthe command to be passed\n\nReturns:\n    :py:class:`dict`: dictionary containing the command to be passed to\n    :meth:`process_run`" ;
    :hasDescription "Process local run dictionary to create the input directory and identify the command to be passed" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :hasSignature "pre_processing()" .

:Function_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator_process_run a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "process_run" ;
    rdfs:comment "Finally launch the code.\n\nRoutine associated to the running of the ``bigdft`` executable.\n\nArguments:\n   command (str): the command as it is set by the ``pre_processing``\n     method.\n\nReturns:\n   :py:class:`dict`: The dictionary containing `timedbg` and `logname`\n     values to be passed to `post_processing` function" ;
    :hasDescription "Finally launch the code." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :hasSignature "process_run(command)" ;
    :hasArgument "command (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_append_run a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "append_run" ;
    rdfs:comment "Add a run into the dataset.\n\nAppend to the list of runs to be performed the corresponding runner and\n   the arguments which are associated to it.\n\nArgs:\n  id (dict): the id of the run, useful to identify the run in the\n     dataset. It has to be a dictionary as it may contain\n     different keyword. For example a run might be classified as\n     ``id = {'hgrid':0.35, 'crmult': 5}``.\n  runner (Runner): the runner class to which the remaining keyword\n     arguments will be passed at the input.\n\nRaises:\n  ValueError: if the provided id is identical to another previously\n     appended run.\n\nTodo:\n   include id in the runs specification" ;
    :hasDescription "Add a run into the dataset." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "append_run(id, runner, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "id (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "runner (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0a567087a54d> .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_fetch_results a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "fetch_results" ;
    rdfs:comment "Retrieve some attribute from some of the results.\n\nSelects out of the results the objects which have in their ``id``\nat least the dictionary specified as input. May return an attribute\nof each result if needed.\n\nArgs:\n   id (dict): dictionary of the retrieved id. Return a list of the runs\n       that have the ``id`` argument inside the provided ``id`` in the\n       order provided by :py:meth:`append_run`.\n       If absent, then the entire list of runs is returned.\n   attribute (str): if present, provide the attribute of each of the\n       results instead of the result object\n   run_if_not_present (bool): If the run has not yet been performed\n       in the dataset then perform it.\n\nExample:\n   >>> study=Dataset()\n   >>> study.append_run(id={'cr': 3}, input={'dft':{'rmult':[3,8]}})\n   >>> study.append_run(id={'cr': 4}, input={'dft':{'rmult':[4,8]}})\n   >>> study.append_run(id={'cr': 3, 'h': 0.5},\n   >>>                  input={'dft':{'hgrids': 0.5, 'rmult':[4,8]}})\n   >>> #append other runs if needed\n   >>> #run the calculations (optional if run_if_not_present=True)\n   >>> study.run()\n   >>> # returns a list of the energies of first and the third result\n   >>> # in this example\n   >>> data=study.fetch_results(id={'cr': 3}, attribute='energy')" ;
    :hasDescription "Retrieve some attribute from some of the results." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "fetch_results(id=None, attribute=None, run_if_not_present=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "id=None" ;
    :hasArgument "attribute=None" ;
    :hasArgument "run_if_not_present=True" ;
    :shownIn <http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0a567087a54d> .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_get_logfiles a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "get_logfiles" ;
    :hasDescription "Method get_logfiles of Dataset (no docstring)." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "get_logfiles()" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_get_times a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "get_times" ;
    :hasDescription "Method get_times of Dataset (no docstring)." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "get_times()" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_post_processing a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "post_processing" ;
    :hasDescription "Calls the Dataset function with the results of the runs as arguments" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "post_processing(**kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_process_run a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "process_run" ;
    rdfs:comment "Run the dataset, by performing explicit run of each of the item of the\n   runs_list." ;
    :hasDescription "Run the dataset, by performing explicit run of each of the item of the runs_list." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "process_run()" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_seek_convergence a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "seek_convergence" ;
    rdfs:comment "Search for the first result of the dataset which matches the provided\ntolerance parameter. The results are in dataset order\n(provided by the :py:meth:`append_run` method) if `selection` is not\nspecified.\nEmploys the numpy :py:meth:`allclose` method for comparison.\n\nArgs:\n  rtol (float): relative tolerance parameter\n  atol (float): absolute tolerance parameter\n  selection (list): list of the id of the runs in which to perform the\n       convergence search. Each id should be unique in the dataset.\n  **kwargs: arguments to be passed to the :py:meth:`fetch_results`\n       method.\n\nReturns:\n  id,result (tuple): the id of the last run which matches the\n        convergence, together with the result, if convergence is\n        reached.\n\nRaises:\n   LookupError: if the parameter for convergence were not found.\n       The dataset has to be enriched or the convergence parameters\n       loosened." ;
    :hasDescription "Search for the first result of the dataset which matches the provided tolerance parameter. The results are in dataset order (provided by the :py:meth:`append_run` method) if `selection` is not specified. Employs the numpy :py:meth:`allclose` method for comparison." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "seek_convergence(rtol=1e-05, atol=1e-08, selection=None, **kwargs)" ;
    :hasArgument "rtol=1e-05" ;
    :hasArgument "atol=1e-08" ;
    :hasArgument "selection=None" ;
    :hasArgument "kwargs (required)" .

:Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_set_postprocessing_function a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "set_postprocessing_function" ;
    rdfs:comment "Set the callback of run.\n\nCalls the function ``func`` after having performed the appended runs.\n\nArgs:\n   func (func): function that process the `inputs` `results` and\n       returns the value of the `run` method of the dataset.\n       The function is called as ``func(self)``." ;
    :hasDescription "Set the callback of run." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :hasSignature "set_postprocessing_function(func)" ;
    :hasArgument "func (required)" .

