:Function_BigDFT_Systems_System_compute_matching a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "compute_matching" ;
    rdfs:comment "Frequently we are passed a list of atom like objects from which we\nneed to extract data and assign it to a system. However, a system\ncan potentially store those atoms in any order, and may not have\nthe same set of atoms. This helper routine creates a mapping between\nthis list view, to the dictionary view of the system class.\n\nArgs:\n  atlist (list): a list of atom like objects.\n  check_matching (bool): if set to True, this will raise an error\n    if we can't match all of the atoms in the system.\n\nReturns:\n  (dict): a mapping from a system to indices in the atom list. If\n    an atom is not in the list, an index value of -1 is assigned." ;
    :hasDescription "Frequently we are passed a list of atom like objects from which we need to extract data and assign it to a system. However, a system can potentially store those atoms in any order, and may not have the same set of atoms. This helper routine creates a mapping between this list view, to the dictionary view of the system class." ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Systems_System ;
    :hasSignature "compute_matching(atlist, check_matching=True)" ;
    :hasArgument "atlist (required)" ;
    :hasArgument "check_matching=True" .

:Function_BigDFT_Systems_System_dataframe_slicing a :Function ;
    rdfs:label "dataframe_slicing" ;
    rdfs:comment "Define a dictionaries of two-element lists indicating the slicing\n(start and end points) of the corresponding fragment in the order\nprovided by the dataframe\n\nArgs:\n    df (Dataframe): associated to the system\n\nReturns:\n    dict:  dictionary of the slicings of the fragments in the dataframe" ;
    :hasDescription "Define a dictionaries of two-element lists indicating the slicing (start and end points) of the corresponding fragment in the order provided by the dataframe" ;
    :methodOf :Class_BigDFT_Systems_System ;
    :hasSignature "dataframe_slicing(df=None)" ;
    :hasArgument "df=None" .

