<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_7543fdcf37ae> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Describe a molecule as a dictionary of positions and pass it to a calculation." ;
    rdfs:comment "The simplest structure PyBigDFT accepts: a dictionary with `units` and a list of one-key dictionaries, element -> [x, y, z]. It goes as `posinp=` to the calculator, which writes it inside NAME.yaml under the key `posinp`." ;
    :hasDescription "Describe a molecule as a dictionary of positions and pass it to a calculation." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "atoms: 3 | orbitals: 4" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Describe a molecule as a dictionary of positions and pass it to a calculation.\n\nThe simplest structure PyBigDFT accepts: a dictionary with `units` and a list of\none-key dictionaries, element -> [x, y, z]. It goes as `posinp=` to the\ncalculator, which writes it inside NAME.yaml under the key `posinp`.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\nwater = {\n    \"units\": \"angstroem\",          # or \"bohr\" (also spelled \"atomic\")\n    \"positions\": [\n        {\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]},\n        {\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]},\n        {\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]},\n    ],\n}\n\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)   # dry run: no SCF\nlog = code.run(name=\"water\", input=Inputfile(), posinp=water, run_dir=\"runs\")\n\nassert log.nat == 3\nprint(\"atoms:\", log.nat, \"| orbitals:\", log.number_of_orbitals)\n" .

:Workflow_Build_a_structure a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Build a structure" ;
    :hasDescription "Build a structure, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_e0ace20bb262> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read a structure from an .xyz file into a System, and turn it into `posinp`." ;
    rdfs:comment "`IO.read_xyz` takes an OPEN FILE, not a file name. `fragmentation` is \"atomic\" (one fragment per atom, the default) or \"single\" (the whole file is one fragment); nothing else is accepted." ;
    :hasDescription "Read a structure from an .xyz file into a System, and turn it into `posinp`." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "fragments: ['FRA:0']\natoms: ['O', 'H', 'H']\n{'H': [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0], 'frag': ['FRA', '0']}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read a structure from an .xyz file into a System, and turn it into `posinp`.\n\n`IO.read_xyz` takes an OPEN FILE, not a file name. `fragmentation` is \"atomic\"\n(one fragment per atom, the default) or \"single\" (the whole file is one\nfragment); nothing else is accepted.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.IO import read_xyz\n\nwith open(\"h2o.xyz\") as ifile:\n    system = read_xyz(ifile, fragmentation=\"single\")\n\nprint(\"fragments:\", list(system.keys()))          # ['FRA:0']\nfragment = system[list(system.keys())[0]]\nprint(\"atoms:\", [atom.sym for atom in fragment])\n\nposinp = system.get_posinp(units=\"angstroem\")     # what `posinp=` of a calculator takes\nassert len(posinp[\"positions\"]) == 3 and posinp[\"units\"] == \"angstroem\"\nprint(posinp[\"positions\"][1])\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_readers_take_open_files ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_structure_file_name_does_not_travel .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0de5af033369> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Give the name of an .xyz file directly as the structure of a calculation." ;
    rdfs:comment "`posinp=` also accepts a file name. The calculator then refers to that file instead of writing the positions in NAME.yaml, so the .xyz must travel with the input: prefer a dictionary (system.get_posinp()) when the input is sent elsewhere." ;
    :hasDescription "Give the name of an .xyz file directly as the structure of a calculation." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "structure read from: h2o.xyz" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Give the name of an .xyz file directly as the structure of a calculation.\n\n`posinp=` also accepts a file name. The calculator then refers to that file\ninstead of writing the positions in NAME.yaml, so the .xyz must travel with the\ninput: prefer a dictionary (system.get_posinp()) when the input is sent elsewhere.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\nlog = code.run(name=\"from_file\", input=Inputfile(), posinp=\"h2o.xyz\")\n\nassert log.nat == 3\nprint(\"structure read from:\", log.posinp_file)\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_structure_file_name_does_not_travel .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_76397a6ec4c2> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Build a System atom by atom, grouped in named fragments." ;
    rdfs:comment "A System is a dictionary of Fragments; a Fragment is a list of Atoms. Fragment names have the form \"NAME:NUMBER\". An Atom is made from a dictionary holding the element as key, its position, and the units of that position." ;
    :hasDescription "Build a System atom by atom, grouped in named fragments." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "valence electrons of the fragment: 8.0\nfirst atom: O [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Build a System atom by atom, grouped in named fragments.\n\nA System is a dictionary of Fragments; a Fragment is a list of Atoms. Fragment\nnames have the form \"NAME:NUMBER\". An Atom is made from a dictionary holding\nthe element as key, its position, and the units of that position.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Atoms import Atom\nfrom BigDFT.Fragments import Fragment\nfrom BigDFT.Systems import System\n\nwater = Fragment([\n    Atom({\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], \"units\": \"angstroem\"}),\n    Atom({\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0], \"units\": \"angstroem\"}),\n    Atom({\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0], \"units\": \"angstroem\"}),\n])\nsystem = System()\nsystem[\"WAT:0\"] = water\n\nposinp = system.get_posinp()                       # angstroem by default\nassert [list(p)[0] for p in posinp[\"positions\"]] == [\"O\", \"H\", \"H\"]\nprint(\"valence electrons of the fragment:\", water.nel)\nprint(\"first atom:\", water[0].sym, water[0].get_position(units=\"angstroem\"))\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_c77befd3bc39> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Take a common molecule from the database shipped with PyBigDFT." ;
    rdfs:comment "`Molecule(name)` is already a `posinp` dictionary (units, positions): pass it as it is to a calculator. It is not a System; build one from its positions when fragments or geometry operations are needed." ;
    :hasDescription "Take a common molecule from the database shipped with PyBigDFT." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "positions: ['O', 'H', 'H']\nas a System, fragments: ['molecule:0']" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Take a common molecule from the database shipped with PyBigDFT.\n\n`Molecule(name)` is already a `posinp` dictionary (units, positions): pass it\nas it is to a calculator. It is not a System; build one from its positions\nwhen fragments or geometry operations are needed.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Database.Molecules import Molecule\nfrom BigDFT.Systems import system_from_dict_positions\n\nposinp = Molecule(\"H2O\")\nassert len(posinp[\"positions\"]) == 3 and posinp[\"units\"] == \"angstroem\"\nprint(\"positions:\", [[k for k in atom if k != \"frag\"][0] for atom in posinp[\"positions\"]])\n\nsystem = system_from_dict_positions(posinp[\"positions\"], units=posinp[\"units\"])\nprint(\"as a System, fragments:\", list(system.keys()))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_molecule_is_not_a_system .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_eec49a6c03fb> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Translate and rotate a fragment, and measure a distance between fragments." ;
    rdfs:comment "Fragment.translate takes a vector in BOHR, whatever the units the atoms were given in. `centroid` is in bohr too. Multiply by AU_to_A to get angstroem." ;
    :hasDescription "Translate and rotate a fragment, and measure a distance between fragments." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "distance between the two molecules: 3.000 angstroem\natoms in the dimer: 6" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Translate and rotate a fragment, and measure a distance between fragments.\n\nFragment.translate takes a vector in BOHR, whatever the units the atoms were\ngiven in. `centroid` is in bohr too. Multiply by AU_to_A to get angstroem.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nimport copy\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom BigDFT.Atoms import AU_to_A\nfrom BigDFT.Fragments import distance\nfrom BigDFT.IO import read_xyz\nfrom BigDFT.Systems import System\n\nwith open(\"h2o.xyz\") as ifile:\n    first = read_xyz(ifile, fragmentation=\"single\")[\"FRA:0\"]\n\nsecond = copy.deepcopy(first)\nsecond.translate([0.0, 0.0, 3.0 / AU_to_A])        # 3 angstroem along z, given in bohr\nsecond.rotate(z=90, units=\"degrees\")\n\ndimer = System()\ndimer[\"WAT:0\"], dimer[\"WAT:1\"] = first, second\n\nd = distance(first, second) * AU_to_A               # between centroids\nassert abs(d - 3.0) < 0.2, d\nprint(\"distance between the two molecules: %.3f angstroem\" % d)\nprint(\"atoms in the dimer:\", len(dimer.get_posinp()[\"positions\"]))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_fragment_geometry_is_in_bohr .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_8732f3f5421d> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Give a periodic cell to a structure: bulk, surface or isolated." ;
    rdfs:comment "The boundary conditions come from the cell, not from an input variable. In a `posinp` dictionary the key `cell` holds the three lengths; a free direction is written `inf` (a surface is periodic along x and z, free along y). No `cell` key at all means an isolated system." ;
    :hasDescription "Give a periodic cell to a structure: bulk, surface or isolated." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "periodic\nsurface\nk-point mesh read by BigDFT: [2, 2, 2]" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Give a periodic cell to a structure: bulk, surface or isolated.\n\nThe boundary conditions come from the cell, not from an input variable. In a\n`posinp` dictionary the key `cell` holds the three lengths; a free direction\nis written `inf` (a surface is periodic along x and z, free along y). No\n`cell` key at all means an isolated system.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\nfrom BigDFT.UnitCells import UnitCell\n\nsilicon = {\n    \"units\": \"angstroem\",\n    \"cell\": [5.43, 5.43, 5.43],                     # periodic in the three directions\n    \"positions\": [{\"Si\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"Si\": [1.3575, 1.3575, 1.3575]}],\n}\nprint(UnitCell([5.43, 5.43, 5.43], units=\"angstroem\").get_boundary_condition().split()[0])\nprint(UnitCell([5.43, float(\"inf\"), 5.43], units=\"angstroem\").get_boundary_condition().split()[0])\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\nassert not hasattr(inp, \"set_kpt_mesh\")                 # PyBigDFT 0.9 has no action for the k-points\ninp[\"kpt\"] = {\"method\": \"mpgrid\", \"ngkpt\": [2, 2, 2]}   # so write the keys\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"si\", input=inp, posinp=silicon, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(\"k-point mesh read by BigDFT:\", log.kpt_mesh)\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_kpt_method ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_kpt_ngkpt ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_no_action_for_kpoints .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_d37a38e696cf> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Write a System to an .xyz file." ;
    rdfs:comment "`IO.write_xyz` takes a System and an OPEN FILE. The first line holds the number of atoms and the units, the second the boundary conditions." ;
    :hasDescription "Write a System to an .xyz file." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "3 angstroem\nfree\nO 0.0 0.0 0.0\nH 0.757 0.5859 0.0\nH -0.757 0.5859 0.0" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Write a System to an .xyz file.\n\n`IO.write_xyz` takes a System and an OPEN FILE. The first line holds the\nnumber of atoms and the units, the second the boundary conditions.\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.IO import read_xyz, write_xyz\n\nwith open(\"h2o.xyz\") as ifile:\n    system = read_xyz(ifile)\n\nwith open(\"copy.xyz\", \"w\") as ofile:\n    write_xyz(system, ofile)\n\nlines = open(\"copy.xyz\").read().splitlines()\nassert lines[0].split()[0] == \"3\" and lines[1].strip() == \"free\"\nprint(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_readers_take_open_files .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_5fb8fd409fbe> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Recover the structure a calculation was run on, from its log." ;
    rdfs:comment "`log.astruct` is the `posinp` dictionary BigDFT read. Build a System from it with system_from_dict_positions. (Systems.system_from_log does the same in one call but imports scipy, which fails in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image of the pack.)" ;
    :hasDescription "Recover the structure a calculation was run on, from its log." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Build_a_structure ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "system_from_log is unusable in this image: libifport.so.5: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\nunits: angstroem | atoms: ['O', 'H', 'H']" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Recover the structure a calculation was run on, from its log.\n\n`log.astruct` is the `posinp` dictionary BigDFT read. Build a System from it\nwith system_from_dict_positions. (Systems.system_from_log does the same in one\ncall but imports scipy, which fails in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image of the pack.)\n\ntask: Build a structure\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\nfrom BigDFT.Systems import system_from_dict_positions\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\nstructure = log.astruct                              # {'units': ..., 'positions': [...]}\nsystem = system_from_dict_positions(structure[\"positions\"], units=structure[\"units\"])\n\nposinp = system.get_posinp()\n\nfrom BigDFT.Systems import system_from_log\ntry:\n    system_from_log(log)\n    raise AssertionError(\"system_from_log works here: use it, and revise this snippet\")\nexcept ImportError as error:\n    print(\"system_from_log is unusable in this image:\", error)\nassert len(posinp[\"positions\"]) == log.nat\nprint(\"units:\", structure[\"units\"], \"| atoms:\", [list(p)[0] for p in structure[\"positions\"]])\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_scipy_cannot_be_imported .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_d97dd4d90e3a> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Write the three settings every calculation needs: functional, grid spacing, extent of the grid." ;
    rdfs:comment "An Inputfile is a dictionary. Its methods (set_xc, set_hgrid, ...) are the functions of BigDFT.InputActions, attached when the object is created: they do not appear in dir(Inputfile). Each one writes one or a few keys; printing the Inputfile shows exactly what BigDFT will read. A key left out keeps BigDFT's default." ;
    :hasDescription "Write the three settings every calculation needs: functional, grid spacing, extent of the grid." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'dft': {'ixc': 'PBE', 'hgrids': 0.4, 'rmult': [5.0, 8.0]}}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Write the three settings every calculation needs: functional, grid spacing, extent of the grid.\n\nAn Inputfile is a dictionary. Its methods (set_xc, set_hgrid, ...) are the\nfunctions of BigDFT.InputActions, attached when the object is created: they do\nnot appear in dir(Inputfile). Each one writes one or a few keys; printing the\nInputfile shows exactly what BigDFT will read. A key left out keeps BigDFT's default.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")                    # dft.ixc. \"LDA\", \"PBE\", \"PBE0\", \"B3LYP\", \"HF\", or a libxc code\ninp.set_hgrid(0.40)                  # dft.hgrids, in bohr. Smaller is more accurate and more expensive\ninp.set_rmult(coarse=5.0, fine=8.0)  # dft.rmult: how far the coarse and fine grids extend around atoms\n\nassert dict(inp) == {\"dft\": {\"ixc\": \"PBE\", \"hgrids\": 0.40, \"rmult\": [5.0, 8.0]}}\nprint(dict(inp))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_input_actions_are_not_in_dir .

:Workflow_Write_an_input_file a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Write an input file" ;
    :hasDescription "Write an input file, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_3632e96e2724> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Set the spin polarisation and the charge of a system." ;
    rdfs:comment "spin_polarize(mpol) writes dft.nspin = 2 and dft.mpol = number of up minus down electrons. charge(q) writes dft.qcharge: +1 for a cation (charge() without argument means -1, an anion). The parity of mpol must match the number of electrons, or BigDFT refuses the input." ;
    :hasDescription "Set the spin polarisation and the charge of a system." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "charge: 1 | nspin: 2 | mpol: 1" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Set the spin polarisation and the charge of a system.\n\nspin_polarize(mpol) writes dft.nspin = 2 and dft.mpol = number of up minus down\nelectrons. charge(q) writes dft.qcharge: +1 for a cation (charge() without\nargument means -1, an anion). The parity of mpol must match the number of\nelectrons, or BigDFT refuses the input.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\nwater = {\"units\": \"angstroem\", \"positions\": [\n    {\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}]}\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.charge(1)                # H2O+: 7 valence electrons\ninp.spin_polarize(mpol=1)    # so one unpaired electron\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"qcharge\"] == 1 and inp[\"dft\"][\"nspin\"] == 2 and inp[\"dft\"][\"mpol\"] == 1\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"cation\", input=inp, posinp=water, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(\"charge:\", log.system_charge, \"| nspin:\", log.spin_polarization, \"| mpol:\", log.total_magn_moment)\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_qcharge ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_nspin ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_mpol ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_odd_electrons_accepted .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_cdacf269201c> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Tighten the self-consistency criterion and allow more iterations." ;
    rdfs:comment "set_scf_convergence(gnrm=...) writes dft.gnrm_cv (default 1e-4). Called WITHOUT a value it writes the string \"default\", not a number. The iteration limits are dft.itermax (50 per cycle) and dft.nrepmax (1 restart): a spin-polarised or difficult system often needs more than 50." ;
    :hasDescription "Tighten the self-consistency criterion and allow more iterations." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'dft': {'gnrm_cv': 1e-05, 'itermax': 200, 'nrepmax': 5}, 'lin_general': {'rpnrm_cv': 'default'}, 'mix': {'rpnrm_cv': 'default'}}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Tighten the self-consistency criterion and allow more iterations.\n\nset_scf_convergence(gnrm=...) writes dft.gnrm_cv (default 1e-4). Called WITHOUT\na value it writes the string \"default\", not a number. The iteration limits are\ndft.itermax (50 per cycle) and dft.nrepmax (1 restart): a spin-polarised or\ndifficult system often needs more than 50.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_scf_convergence(gnrm=1.0e-5)\ninp[\"dft\"].update(itermax=200, nrepmax=5)     # no action takes these two as plain numbers\n\nassert inp[\"dft\"] == {\"gnrm_cv\": 1.0e-5, \"itermax\": 200, \"nrepmax\": 5}\nprint(dict(inp))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_scf_convergence_default_is_a_string .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_78e7e064413d> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Ask for a geometry optimisation." ;
    rdfs:comment "optimize_geometry writes the `geopt` section. Its default method is FIRE with 50 steps and forcemax = 0, which means \"stop on the fluctuation of the forces\": give forcemax (Ha/bohr) explicitly. SQNM is the usual choice for molecules." ;
    :hasDescription "Ask for a geometry optimisation." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'method': 'SQNM', 'ncount_cluster_x': 100, 'betax': 4.0, 'frac_fluct': 1.0, 'forcemax': 0.001}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Ask for a geometry optimisation.\n\noptimize_geometry writes the `geopt` section. Its default method is FIRE with\n50 steps and forcemax = 0, which means \"stop on the fluctuation of the forces\":\ngive forcemax (Ha/bohr) explicitly. SQNM is the usual choice for molecules.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\nwater = {\"units\": \"angstroem\", \"positions\": [\n    {\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}]}\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.optimize_geometry(method=\"SQNM\", nsteps=100, forcemax=1.0e-3)\nassert inp[\"geopt\"][\"method\"] == \"SQNM\" and inp[\"geopt\"][\"ncount_cluster_x\"] == 100\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"relax\", input=inp, posinp=water, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(inp[\"geopt\"])\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_geopt_method ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_geopt_ncount_cluster_x ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_geometry_optimisation_defaults .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_4b96ec8088d3> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Use a hybrid functional (PBE0, B3LYP, HF): name the pseudopotentials explicitly." ;
    rdfs:comment "BigDFT has no pseudopotential registered for a hybrid functional. With set_xc(\"PBE0\") alone it refuses the input: 'The pseudopotential parameter file \"psppar.O\" is lacking, and no registered pseudo found for \"O\"'. Tell it to use the PBE ones (XC code 11), for every element of the structure. BigDFT then warns that the pseudopotential was generated with another functional." ;
    :hasDescription "Use a hybrid functional (PBE0, B3LYP, HF): name the pseudopotentials explicitly." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "STOP  MPIFAKE: MPI_ABORT\nwithout pseudopotentials: The pseudopotential parameter file \"psppar.O\" is lacking, and no registered pseudo found for \"O\"\nwith the PBE pseudopotentials: dry run passed, memory peak 86 MB" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Use a hybrid functional (PBE0, B3LYP, HF): name the pseudopotentials explicitly.\n\nBigDFT has no pseudopotential registered for a hybrid functional. With\nset_xc(\"PBE0\") alone it refuses the input: 'The pseudopotential parameter file\n\"psppar.O\" is lacking, and no registered pseudo found for \"O\"'. Tell it to use\nthe PBE ones (XC code 11), for every element of the structure. BigDFT then\nwarns that the pseudopotential was generated with another functional.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\nwater = {\"units\": \"angstroem\", \"positions\": [\n    {\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}]}\nelements = sorted({element for atom in water[\"positions\"] for element in atom})\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE0\")\nrefused = code.run(name=\"pbe0_refused\", input=inp, posinp=water, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert \"Additional Info\" in refused.log                     # BigDFT refused it: this key holds the reason\nprint(\"without pseudopotentials:\", refused.log[\"Additional Info\"])\n\nfor element in elements:\n    inp[\"psppar.\" + element] = {\"Pseudopotential XC\": 11}   # 11 = PBE\naccepted = code.run(name=\"pbe0\", input=inp, posinp=water, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert \"Additional Info\" not in accepted.log\nprint(\"with the PBE pseudopotentials: dry run passed, memory peak\", accepted.memory_peak, \"MB\")\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_never_raises ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_hybrid_needs_pseudopotential .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_dd92f39d71c0> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Set an input variable that no action covers, by writing its key." ;
    rdfs:comment "The Inputfile is a dictionary of sections. Any variable of BigDFT can be written as inp[section][key] = value; create the section first if it is not there. Actions and direct keys mix freely. A wrong key name is NOT refused by PyBigDFT: only BigDFT (the dry run) tells." ;
    :hasDescription "Set an input variable that no action covers, by writing its key." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "ncong read by BigDFT: 8 | alphamix: 0.3" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Set an input variable that no action covers, by writing its key.\n\nThe Inputfile is a dictionary of sections. Any variable of BigDFT can be\nwritten as inp[section][key] = value; create the section first if it is not\nthere. Actions and direct keys mix freely. A wrong key name is NOT refused by\nPyBigDFT: only BigDFT (the dry run) tells.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp[\"dft\"][\"ncong\"] = 8                                   # the section exists: set_xc created it\ninp.setdefault(\"mix\", {})[\"alphamix\"] = 0.3               # a section that may not exist yet\ninp[\"perf\"] = {\"multipole_preserving\": True}              # a new section, written whole\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"keys\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nassert log.log[\"dft\"][\"ncong\"] == 8                       # BigDFT read it: the log repeats the input\nprint(\"ncong read by BigDFT:\", log.log[\"dft\"][\"ncong\"], \"| alphamix:\", log.log[\"mix\"][\"alphamix\"])\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_ncong ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_perf_multipole_preserving .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_e6334eb746ee> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Compute in implicit solvent (soft-sphere cavity)." ;
    rdfs:comment "set_implicit_solvent() switches the cavity on with the parameters of water. It takes no solvent name in PyBigDFT 0.9: another solvent is set by writing the keys of psolver.environment (epsilon, and the cavity parameters)." ;
    :hasDescription "Compute in implicit solvent (soft-sphere cavity)." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "no solvent name: set_implicit_solvent() got an unexpected keyword argument 'solvent'\ncavity: soft-sphere | epsilon: 24.852" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Compute in implicit solvent (soft-sphere cavity).\n\nset_implicit_solvent() switches the cavity on with the parameters of water. It\ntakes no solvent name in PyBigDFT 0.9: another solvent is set by writing the\nkeys of psolver.environment (epsilon, and the cavity parameters).\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.set_implicit_solvent()\ntry:\n    Inputfile().set_implicit_solvent(solvent=\"ethanol\")\n    raise AssertionError(\"this version accepts a solvent name: revise this snippet\")\nexcept TypeError as error:\n    print(\"no solvent name:\", error)\nassert inp[\"psolver\"][\"environment\"][\"cavity\"] == \"soft-sphere\"\n\ninp[\"psolver\"][\"environment\"][\"epsilon\"] = 24.852          # ethanol instead of water (78.36)\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"solvated\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(\"cavity:\", log.log[\"psolver\"][\"environment\"][\"cavity\"],\n      \"| epsilon:\", log.log[\"psolver\"][\"environment\"][\"epsilon\"])\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_implicit_solvent_takes_no_solvent_name .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0d92b27b3bc7> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Add an electric field, a dispersion correction, or an electronic temperature." ;
    rdfs:comment "Three independent actions, each writing one key. The field is in atomic units (Ha/bohr). The dispersion correction (D3) only exists for isolated systems." ;
    :hasDescription "Add an electric field, a dispersion correction, or an electronic temperature." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'dft': {'elecfield': [0.0, 0.0, 0.001], 'dispersion': 5}, 'mix': {'tel': 0.001}}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Add an electric field, a dispersion correction, or an electronic temperature.\n\nThree independent actions, each writing one key. The field is in atomic units\n(Ha/bohr). The dispersion correction (D3) only exists for isolated systems.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.apply_electric_field([0.0, 0.0, 1.0e-3])   # dft.elecfield\ninp.set_dispersion_correction()                # dft.dispersion = 5 (Grimme D3)\ninp.set_electronic_temperature(kT=1.0e-3)      # mix.tel, in hartree; or T=300 in kelvin\n\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"elecfield\"] == [0.0, 0.0, 1.0e-3]\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"dispersion\"] == 5 and inp[\"mix\"][\"tel\"] == 1.0e-3\nprint(dict(inp))\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_elecfield ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_dispersion ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_mix_tel .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_fbfe5297dec3> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Ask BigDFT to write the density, the orbitals or cube files." ;
    rdfs:comment "These actions choose what a run leaves in data-NAME/ besides its log." ;
    :hasDescription "Ask BigDFT to write the density, the orbitals or cube files." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'dft': {'output_denspot': 21, 'nplot': 2}, 'output': {'orbitals': 'binary'}}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Ask BigDFT to write the density, the orbitals or cube files.\n\nThese actions choose what a run leaves in data-NAME/ besides its log.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.write_density_on_disk()                     # dft.output_denspot = 21: density as a cube file\ninp.write_orbitals_on_disk()                    # output.orbitals = binary: one file per orbital\ninp.write_cubefiles_around_fermi_level(nplot=2) # dft.nplot: cube files of the orbitals near the gap\n\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"output_denspot\"] == 21 and inp[\"dft\"][\"nplot\"] == 2\nassert inp[\"output\"][\"orbitals\"] == \"binary\"\nprint(dict(inp))\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_output_denspot ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_nplot ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_output_orbitals .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_b6431fe0ec3f> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Save an Inputfile to YAML and load it back." ;
    rdfs:comment "An Inputfile is a dictionary: yaml.dump writes it, Inputfile(dictionary) reads it. The file NAME.yaml that a calculator writes is the same thing plus `posinp`." ;
    :hasDescription "Save an Inputfile to YAML and load it back." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "prepare" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "dft:\n  hgrids: 0.4\n  ixc: PBE" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Save an Inputfile to YAML and load it back.\n\nAn Inputfile is a dictionary: yaml.dump writes it, Inputfile(dictionary) reads\nit. The file NAME.yaml that a calculator writes is the same thing plus `posinp`.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: prepare\n\"\"\"\nimport yaml\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.set_hgrid(0.4)\nwith open(\"settings.yaml\", \"w\") as f:\n    yaml.dump(dict(inp), f, default_flow_style=False)\n\nwith open(\"settings.yaml\") as f:\n    again = Inputfile(yaml.safe_load(f))\nagain.spin_polarize(mpol=2)                      # the actions are there on the reloaded object\n\nassert again[\"dft\"][\"ixc\"] == \"PBE\" and again[\"dft\"][\"nspin\"] == 2\nprint(open(\"settings.yaml\").read().strip())\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_ixc ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_nspin ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_input_actions_are_not_in_dir .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_bf30c1d1507e> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Compute empty (virtual) orbitals, for a gap or a density of states above the Fermi level." ;
    rdfs:comment "extract_virtual_states(nvirt) writes dft.nvirt and dft.norbv. Without it a log only holds the occupied levels." ;
    :hasDescription "Compute empty (virtual) orbitals, for a gap or a density of states above the Fermi level." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "{'ixc': 'PBE', 'norbv': -4, 'nvirt': 4, 'itermax_virt': 150}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Compute empty (virtual) orbitals, for a gap or a density of states above the Fermi level.\n\nextract_virtual_states(nvirt) writes dft.nvirt and dft.norbv. Without it a log\nonly holds the occupied levels.\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.extract_virtual_states(nvirt=4)\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"nvirt\"] == 4\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"virtual\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(inp[\"dft\"])\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_nvirt .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_8e63561339da> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Dry-run an input and decide, correctly, whether BigDFT accepted it." ;
    rdfs:comment "A dry run (SystemCalculator(dry_run=True)) makes BigDFT read the input and build the grid, without any SCF step. It writes NAME.yaml, the file a real run reads. PyBigDFT returns a Logfile and raises nothing, WHATEVER BigDFT said. Three outcomes, all read in log.log: - refused: the key \"Additional Info\" is at the top of the log, with the reason; - accepted with errors: \"List of error found while parsing input variables\" is there. BigDFT went on although a value is out of range or not allowed; - accepted: neither key. Warnings, if any, are under \"WARNINGS\". The memory estimate (log.memory_peak) is only printed for the cubic algorithm: do not use it as the test." ;
    :hasDescription "Dry-run an input and decide, correctly, whether BigDFT accepted it." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Check_an_input_before_computing ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "STOP  MPIFAKE: MPI_ABORT\nSTOP  MPIFAKE: MPI_ABORT\ngood        : accepted\nodd         : accepted, warnings: ['Odd number of electrons, no closed shell system']\nhybrid      : refused, The pseudopotential parameter file \"psppar.O\" is lacking, and no registered pseudo found for \"O\"\ntypo        : refused, An invalid key (hgrid) has been found in section \"dft\". Check above the allowed keys.\nout of range: accepted WITH ERRORS, hgrids = '9.0' not in range." ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Dry-run an input and decide, correctly, whether BigDFT accepted it.\n\nA dry run (SystemCalculator(dry_run=True)) makes BigDFT read the input and\nbuild the grid, without any SCF step. It writes NAME.yaml, the file a real run\nreads. PyBigDFT returns a Logfile and raises nothing, WHATEVER BigDFT said.\nThree outcomes, all read in log.log:\n  - refused: the key \"Additional Info\" is at the top of the log, with the reason;\n  - accepted with errors: \"List of error found while parsing input variables\"\n    is there. BigDFT went on although a value is out of range or not allowed;\n  - accepted: neither key. Warnings, if any, are under \"WARNINGS\".\nThe memory estimate (log.memory_peak) is only printed for the cubic algorithm:\ndo not use it as the test.\n\ntask: Check an input before computing\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\n\ndef dry_run(name, inp, posinp, run_dir=\"runs\"):\n    \"\"\"Return (status, details). status is \"accepted\", \"errors\" or \"refused\".\"\"\"\n    code = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\n    doc = code.run(name=name, input=inp, posinp=posinp, run_dir=run_dir).log\n    if \"Additional Info\" in doc:\n        return \"refused\", [doc[\"Additional Info\"]]\n    errors = doc.get(\"List of error found while parsing input variables\")\n    if errors:\n        return \"errors\", [e[\"Additional Info\"] for e in errors]\n    return \"accepted\", [str(w) for w in (doc.get(\"WARNINGS\") or [])]\n\n\ngood = Inputfile()\ngood.set_xc(\"PBE\")\nassert dry_run(\"good\", good, \"h2o.xyz\") == (\"accepted\", [])\nprint(\"good        : accepted\")\n\nodd = Inputfile()\nodd.charge(1)                               # 7 electrons and no spin polarisation\nstatus, details = dry_run(\"odd\", odd, \"h2o.xyz\")\nassert status == \"accepted\" and details     # accepted, but BigDFT warns\nprint(\"odd         : accepted, warnings:\", details)\n\nhybrid = Inputfile()\nhybrid.set_xc(\"PBE0\")                       # no pseudopotential registered for a hybrid\nstatus, details = dry_run(\"hybrid\", hybrid, \"h2o.xyz\")\nassert status == \"refused\"\nprint(\"hybrid      : refused,\", details[0])\n\ntypo = Inputfile({\"dft\": {\"hgrid\": 0.4}})   # the key is hgrids\nstatus, details = dry_run(\"typo\", typo, \"h2o.xyz\")\nassert status == \"refused\"\nprint(\"typo        : refused,\", details[0])\n\ncoarse = Inputfile()\ncoarse.set_hgrid(9.0)                       # out of range: BigDFT says so and goes on\nstatus, details = dry_run(\"coarse\", coarse, \"h2o.xyz\")\nassert status == \"errors\"\nprint(\"out of range: accepted WITH ERRORS,\", details[0])\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_never_raises ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_accepts_input_errors ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_memory_estimate_absent_in_linear_scaling ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_odd_electrons_accepted .

:Workflow_Check_an_input_before_computing a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Check an input before computing" ;
    :hasDescription "Check an input before computing, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_ab6f691cfd10> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Never dry-run under the name of a calculation that is already done." ;
    rdfs:comment "A dry run writes log-NAME.yaml, like a real run. Under the same name and in the same directory it REPLACES the log of the finished calculation, and the energy is gone. `skip=True` does not protect: with dry_run=True the estimate runs anyway. Test for a finished calculation yourself before preparing it again." ;
    :hasDescription "Never dry-run under the name of a calculation that is already done." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Check_an_input_before_computing ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "<BigDFT> Logfile existing, renamed into: ./logfiles/log-h2o.14:26:31.617.yaml\nbefore: energy -17.20985643099385\nafter : log-h2o.yaml is now a dry-run log, without energy" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Never dry-run under the name of a calculation that is already done.\n\nA dry run writes log-NAME.yaml, like a real run. Under the same name and in the\nsame directory it REPLACES the log of the finished calculation, and the energy\nis gone. `skip=True` does not protect: with dry_run=True the estimate runs\nanyway. Test for a finished calculation yourself before preparing it again.\n\ntask: Check an input before computing\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nimport os\n\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\n\ndef is_computed(name, run_dir=\".\"):\n    \"\"\"True if log-NAME.yaml holds a finished calculation, not a dry run or a refusal.\"\"\"\n    path = os.path.join(run_dir, \"log-%s.yaml\" % name)\n    if not os.path.isfile(path):\n        return False\n    try:\n        log = Logfile(path)\n        last = log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1]\n        return getattr(last, \"energy\", None) is not None\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\n\nassert is_computed(\"h2o\")                        # the finished run of the fixtures\nprint(\"before: energy\", Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\").energy)\n\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, skip=True, verbose=False)\ncode.run(name=\"h2o\", input=Inputfile(), posinp=\"h2o.xyz\")     # same name, same directory\n\nassert not is_computed(\"h2o\")                    # the result has been overwritten\nprint(\"after : log-h2o.yaml is now a dry-run log, without energy\")\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_overwrites_log ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_log_attributes_may_be_absent .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_182ecc95f18d> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Prepare several runs for the HAPS: one NAME.yaml each, dry-run, names it accepts." ;
    rdfs:comment "The HAPS runs `bigdft -n NAME` on NAME.yaml and nothing else. So: write every input with a dry run in one directory, keep the names that passed, and hand them to haps_bigdft(names=[...], directory=\"runs\"). A run name may only hold letters, digits, '_' and '-' (no dot, no colon), 64 characters at most." ;
    :hasDescription "Prepare several runs for the HAPS: one NAME.yaml each, dry-run, names it accepts." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Send_runs_to_the_HAPS ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "ready for the HAPS: ['water_h050', 'water_h045', 'water_h040']\nnext: haps_bigdft(names=['water_h050', 'water_h045', 'water_h040'], directory=\"runs\")" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Prepare several runs for the HAPS: one NAME.yaml each, dry-run, names it accepts.\n\nThe HAPS runs `bigdft -n NAME` on NAME.yaml and nothing else. So: write every\ninput with a dry run in one directory, keep the names that passed, and hand\nthem to haps_bigdft(names=[...], directory=\"runs\"). A run name may only hold\nletters, digits, '_' and '-' (no dot, no colon), 64 characters at most.\n\ntask: Send runs to the HAPS\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nimport re\n\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\nNAME = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,63}$\")\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\nready, refused = [], {}\n\nfor hgrid in (0.50, 0.45, 0.40):\n    name = \"water_h%03d\" % round(hgrid * 100)        # water_h050: not \"h=0.5\", not \"h:0.5\"\n    assert NAME.match(name), name\n    inp = Inputfile()\n    inp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\n    inp.set_hgrid(hgrid)\n    log = code.run(name=name, input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\n    problems = log.log.get(\"Additional Info\") or log.log.get(\"List of error found while parsing input variables\")\n    if problems:\n        refused[name] = problems                     # refused, or accepted with an input error: do not send\n    else:\n        ready.append(name)\n\nassert ready == [\"water_h050\", \"water_h045\", \"water_h040\"] and not refused\nprint(\"ready for the HAPS:\", ready)\nprint('next: haps_bigdft(names=%r, directory=\"runs\")' % ready)\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_never_raises ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_accepts_input_errors ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dataset_names_not_accepted_by_haps .

:Workflow_Send_runs_to_the_HAPS a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Send runs to the HAPS" ;
    :hasDescription "Send runs to the HAPS, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_0a567087a54d> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Group runs in a Dataset and collect one quantity from all of them." ;
    rdfs:comment "A Dataset holds runs identified by a dictionary (`id`). `run()` executes them with the calculator given to append_run, `fetch_results(attribute=...)` returns the attribute of every log, in order. The run names are built from the ids (\"h:0.5\"): they contain ':' and '.', which the HAPS does not accept. Use a Dataset for dry runs and local runs; name the runs yourself for the HAPS." ;
    :hasDescription "Group runs in a Dataset and collect one quantity from all of them." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Converge_a_parameter ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "<BigDFT> Logfile existing, renamed into: ./logfiles/log-h:0.5.14:26:33.062.yaml\n <BigDFT> Logfile existing, renamed into: ./logfiles/log-h:0.45.14:26:33.184.yaml\n <BigDFT> Logfile existing, renamed into: ./logfiles/log-h:0.4.14:26:33.317.yaml\nnames : ['h:0.5', 'h:0.45', 'h:0.4']\nmemory: [70, 86, 117] MB" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Group runs in a Dataset and collect one quantity from all of them.\n\nA Dataset holds runs identified by a dictionary (`id`). `run()` executes them\nwith the calculator given to append_run, `fetch_results(attribute=...)` returns\nthe attribute of every log, in order. The run names are built from the ids\n(\"h:0.5\"): they contain ':' and '.', which the HAPS does not accept. Use a\nDataset for dry runs and local runs; name the runs yourself for the HAPS.\n\ntask: Converge a parameter\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Datasets import Dataset\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\nstudy = Dataset(label=\"grid\", run_dir=\"grid\")\nfor hgrid in (0.50, 0.45, 0.40):\n    inp = Inputfile()\n    inp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\n    inp.set_hgrid(hgrid)\n    study.append_run(id={\"h\": hgrid}, runner=code, input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\")\n\nstudy.run()\nmemory = study.fetch_results(attribute=\"memory_peak\")\n\nassert study.names == [\"h:0.5\", \"h:0.45\", \"h:0.4\"] and len(memory) == 3\nprint(\"names :\", study.names)\nprint(\"memory:\", memory, \"MB\")\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dataset_names_not_accepted_by_haps .

:Workflow_Converge_a_parameter a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Converge a parameter" ;
    :hasDescription "Converge a parameter, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_77952689a33e> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Run a calculation directly, where the bigdft executable is available." ;
    rdfs:comment "Without dry_run the calculator launches BigDFT and returns the log of the finished run. In the pack's container bigdft is disabled: there, prepare with a dry run and send the name to the HAPS instead. `omp` is the number of OpenMP threads (a string); `mpi_run` is the launcher prefix, e.g. \"mpirun -np 2\"." ;
    :hasDescription "Run a calculation directly, where the bigdft executable is available." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Send_runs_to_the_HAPS ;
    :runsAtStage "compute" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "energy: -17.200235 Ha" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Run a calculation directly, where the bigdft executable is available.\n\nWithout dry_run the calculator launches BigDFT and returns the log of the\nfinished run. In the pack's container bigdft is disabled: there, prepare with a\ndry run and send the name to the HAPS instead. `omp` is the number of OpenMP\nthreads (a string); `mpi_run` is the launcher prefix, e.g. \"mpirun -np 2\".\n\ntask: Send runs to the HAPS\nstage: compute\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.set_hgrid(0.5)\n\ncode = SystemCalculator(omp=\"2\", verbose=False)\nlog = code.run(name=\"direct\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\n\nassert abs(log.energy + 17.2) < 0.05\nprint(\"energy: %.6f Ha\" % log.energy)\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_940db71e3fce> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Switch to the linear-scaling algorithm, for systems of hundreds of atoms and more." ;
    rdfs:comment "set_linear_scaling() writes dft.inputpsiid = \"linear\". A dry run of such an input is accepted but prints NO memory estimate: log.memory_peak is absent. So \"no memory estimate\" does not mean \"refused\"; look for \"Additional Info\"." ;
    :hasDescription "Switch to the linear-scaling algorithm, for systems of hundreds of atoms and more." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Write_an_input_file ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "At line 1677 of file /opt/bigdft/bigdft/src/modules/types.f90\nFortran runtime error: Attempt to DEALLOCATE unallocated 'aux'\n\nError termination. Backtrace:\n#0  0x7f9c8f3f5d21 in ???\n#1  0x7f9c8f3f6869 in ???\n#2  0x7f9c8f3f6ee6 in ???\n#3  0x7f9c8fb1dd88 in ???\n#4  0x7f9c8fb1deb8 in ???\n#5  0x7f9c8f816f9d in ???\n#6  0x7f9c8f8fb44b in ???\n#7  0x7f9c8f90371a in ???\n#8  0x56409797955d in ???\n#9  0x564097971a4e in ???\n#10  0x7f9c871d20b2 in ???\n#11  0x564097971a8d in ???\n#12  0xffffffffffffffff in ???\naccepted; memory estimate: not printed in linear scaling" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Switch to the linear-scaling algorithm, for systems of hundreds of atoms and more.\n\nset_linear_scaling() writes dft.inputpsiid = \"linear\". A dry run of such an\ninput is accepted but prints NO memory estimate: log.memory_peak is absent. So\n\"no memory estimate\" does not mean \"refused\"; look for \"Additional Info\".\n\ntask: Write an input file\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\ninp.set_linear_scaling()\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"inputpsiid\"] == \"linear\"\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"linear\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\", run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert \"Additional Info\" not in log.log                 # accepted\nassert getattr(log, \"memory_peak\", None) is None        # and yet no estimate\nprint(\"accepted; memory estimate:\", getattr(log, \"memory_peak\", \"not printed in linear scaling\"))\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_inputpsiid ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_memory_estimate_absent_in_linear_scaling .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_90e6dfaaa9a3> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read the energy and the main quantities of a finished calculation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Logfile(path) loads log-NAME.yaml. Its attributes (energy, nat, fermi_level, dipole, forces, evals, memory_peak, ...) are created from the content of the log: one that BigDFT did not write is simply ABSENT, so use getattr with a default. Energies are in hartree; BigDFT.DoS.AU_eV converts to eV." ;
    :hasDescription "Read the energy and the main quantities of a finished calculation." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "energy          : -17.20985643 Ha = -468.3040 eV\natoms, orbitals : 3 4\nhighest occupied: -0.2657 Ha\ndipole (AU)     : [-0.0001, 0.701, -0.0007]\nmemory peak     : 86 MB\npressure        : not in this log" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read the energy and the main quantities of a finished calculation.\n\nLogfile(path) loads log-NAME.yaml. Its attributes (energy, nat, fermi_level,\ndipole, forces, evals, memory_peak, ...) are created from the content of the\nlog: one that BigDFT did not write is simply ABSENT, so use getattr with a\ndefault. Energies are in hartree; BigDFT.DoS.AU_eV converts to eV.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.DoS import AU_eV\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\n\nprint(\"energy          : %.8f Ha = %.4f eV\" % (log.energy, log.energy * AU_eV))\nprint(\"atoms, orbitals :\", log.nat, log.number_of_orbitals)\nprint(\"highest occupied: %.4f Ha\" % log.fermi_level)\nprint(\"dipole (AU)     :\", [round(x, 4) for x in log.dipole])\nprint(\"memory peak     :\", log.memory_peak, \"MB\")\nprint(\"pressure        :\", getattr(log, \"pressure\", \"not in this log\"))   # only for periodic systems\n\nassert abs(log.energy + 17.21) < 0.01 and log.nat == 3\nassert not hasattr(log, \"pressure\")\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_log_attributes_may_be_absent .

:Workflow_Read_a_result a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Read a result" ;
    :hasDescription "Read a result, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_494dcb5bb347> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Check that a finished run converged, and collect what BigDFT warned about." ;
    rdfs:comment "Three things to look at: the last wavefunction residue against the criterion (dft.gnrm_cv), the warnings (log.log[\"WARNINGS\"], absent or None when there are none), and that an energy is there at all. A run can end normally, report convergence, and still carry warnings worth reading." ;
    :hasDescription "Check that a finished run converged, and collect what BigDFT warned about." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "h2o          : 11 iterations, residue 7.0e-05 <= 1.0e-04\npbe0_restart : 8 iterations, warnings: ['PSP generated with a different XC. Input XC is \"XC: PBEH (PBE0)\"']" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Check that a finished run converged, and collect what BigDFT warned about.\n\nThree things to look at: the last wavefunction residue against the criterion\n(dft.gnrm_cv), the warnings (log.log[\"WARNINGS\"], absent or None when there are\nnone), and that an energy is there at all. A run can end normally, report\nconvergence, and still carry warnings worth reading.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile, find_iterations\n\n\ndef verdict(path):\n    log = Logfile(path)\n    residues = find_iterations(log.log)            # one row per SCF cycle, the residue at each iteration\n    last, iterations = float(residues[-1][-1]), int(sum(len(row) for row in residues))\n    warnings = [w if isinstance(w, str) else \" \".join(\"%s: %s\" % kv for kv in w.items())\n                for w in (log.log.get(\"WARNINGS\") or [])]\n    return {\"energy\": getattr(log, \"energy\", None), \"iterations\": iterations, \"last_residue\": last,\n            \"criterion\": log.gnrm_cv, \"converged\": last <= log.gnrm_cv, \"warnings\": warnings}\n\n\nclean = verdict(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\nassert clean[\"converged\"] and clean[\"warnings\"] == []\nprint(\"h2o          :\", clean[\"iterations\"], \"iterations, residue %.1e <= %.1e\" % (clean[\"last_residue\"], clean[\"criterion\"]))\n\nwarned = verdict(\"log-pbe0_restart.yaml\")\nassert warned[\"converged\"] and len(warned[\"warnings\"]) == 1\nprint(\"pbe0_restart :\", warned[\"iterations\"], \"iterations, warnings:\", warned[\"warnings\"])\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_eb9431b43940> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read a geometry optimisation: take the LAST step, not the attributes of the log." ;
    rdfs:comment "The log of a relaxation holds one document per force evaluation: len(log) is their number (0 for a single point) and log[i] is step i. The attributes of the log itself (log.energy, log.forcemax) are those of the step of LOWEST ENERGY (log.reference_log), which is not necessarily the last one nor the one whose geometry BigDFT wrote in final_NAME.yaml." ;
    :hasDescription "Read a geometry optimisation: take the LAST step, not the attributes of the log." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "Found 16 different runs\nforce evaluations      : 16\nenergy of the last step: -17.21121191 Ha, largest force 1.70e-04 Ha/bohr\nlog.energy             : -17.21124578 Ha, which is step 9\nenergy gained          : 1.36 mHa\nFound 16 different runs" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read a geometry optimisation: take the LAST step, not the attributes of the log.\n\nThe log of a relaxation holds one document per force evaluation: len(log) is\ntheir number (0 for a single point) and log[i] is step i. The attributes of the\nlog itself (log.energy, log.forcemax) are those of the step of LOWEST ENERGY\n(log.reference_log), which is not necessarily the last one nor the one whose\ngeometry BigDFT wrote in final_NAME.yaml.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o_relax.yaml\")\nsteps = [log[i] for i in range(len(log))]\nlast = steps[-1]\n\nprint(\"force evaluations      :\", len(steps))\nprint(\"energy of the last step: %.8f Ha, largest force %.2e Ha/bohr\" % (last.energy, last.forcemax))\nprint(\"log.energy             : %.8f Ha, which is step %d\" % (log.energy, log.reference_log))\nprint(\"energy gained          : %.2f mHa\" % ((steps[0].energy - last.energy) * 1000))\n\nassert len(log) > 1\nassert log.energy == min(s.energy for s in steps)          # the lowest, not the last\nassert last.forcemax <= 1.0e-3                              # the criterion asked in the input\n\n\ndef final_energy(path):\n    \"\"\"Energy of a run, single point or relaxation alike.\"\"\"\n    log = Logfile(path)\n    return (log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1]).energy\n\n\nassert final_energy(\"log-h2o_relax.yaml\") == last.energy\nassert final_energy(\"log-h2o.yaml\") == Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\").energy\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_relaxation_attributes_are_lowest_energy .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_d6f6eae07786> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Start a calculation from the geometry a relaxation ended on." ;
    rdfs:comment "BigDFT writes the final geometry in final_NAME.yaml (same directory as the log), with the forces on each atom. Keep the element and its position, drop the rest, and the result is a `posinp` dictionary for the next run." ;
    :hasDescription "Start a calculation from the geometry a relaxation ended on." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Chain_calculations ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "O-H distance after relaxation: 0.9779 angstroem" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Start a calculation from the geometry a relaxation ended on.\n\nBigDFT writes the final geometry in final_NAME.yaml (same directory as the\nlog), with the forces on each atom. Keep the element and its position, drop\nthe rest, and the result is a `posinp` dictionary for the next run.\n\ntask: Chain calculations\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nimport yaml\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\n\ndef relaxed(name, run_dir=\".\"):\n    \"\"\"The geometry BigDFT wrote at the end of the relaxation NAME, as a posinp dictionary.\"\"\"\n    with open(\"%s/final_%s.yaml\" % (run_dir, name)) as f:\n        final = yaml.safe_load(f)\n    positions = [{element: xyz for element, xyz in atom.items() if element != \"force\"}\n                 for atom in final[\"positions\"]]\n    return {\"units\": final.get(\"units\", \"angstroem\"), \"positions\": positions}\n\n\nposinp = relaxed(\"h2o_relax\")\nassert [list(atom)[0] for atom in posinp[\"positions\"]] == [\"O\", \"H\", \"H\"]\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"after_relax\", input=inp, posinp=posinp, run_dir=\"runs\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(\"O-H distance after relaxation: %.4f angstroem\"\n      % sum((a - b) ** 2 for a, b in zip(posinp[\"positions\"][0][\"O\"], posinp[\"positions\"][1][\"H\"])) ** 0.5)\n" .

:Workflow_Chain_calculations a :Workflow ;
    rdfs:label "Chain calculations" ;
    :hasDescription "Chain calculations, with PyBigDFT: the snippets that show how." .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_fef6feefdaa1> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read the orbital energies: highest occupied level, and both spins of a polarised system." ;
    rdfs:comment "log.evals is a list with one BandArray per k-point. A BandArray is a numpy array of shape (number of spins, number of orbitals), in hartree. With spin polarisation the two rows may hold different numbers of orbitals: the shorter one is padded with nan. A log only holds occupied orbitals unless virtual states were asked for (extract_virtual_states)." ;
    :hasDescription "Read the orbital energies: highest occupied level, and both spins of a polarised system." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "water, occupied levels (eV): [-25.457, -13.183, -9.287, -7.23]\nwater, highest occupied    : -7.230 eV\nOH, highest occupied up    : -7.934 eV\nOH, highest occupied down  : -7.337 eV" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read the orbital energies: highest occupied level, and both spins of a polarised system.\n\nlog.evals is a list with one BandArray per k-point. A BandArray is a numpy\narray of shape (number of spins, number of orbitals), in hartree. With spin\npolarisation the two rows may hold different numbers of orbitals: the shorter\none is padded with nan. A log only holds occupied orbitals unless virtual\nstates were asked for (extract_virtual_states).\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom BigDFT.DoS import AU_eV\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nclosed = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\").evals[0]            # first (only) k-point\nassert closed.shape == (1, 4)\nprint(\"water, occupied levels (eV):\", np.round(closed[0] * AU_eV, 3).tolist())\nprint(\"water, highest occupied    : %.3f eV\" % (closed[0].max() * AU_eV))\n\nradical = Logfile(\"log-oh.yaml\").evals[0]            # OH: 4 up, 3 down\nup, down = radical[0], radical[1][~np.isnan(radical[1])]\nassert radical.shape == (2, 4) and len(up) == 4 and len(down) == 3\nprint(\"OH, highest occupied up    : %.3f eV\" % (up.max() * AU_eV))\nprint(\"OH, highest occupied down  : %.3f eV\" % (down.max() * AU_eV))\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_orbital_energies_are_padded_with_nan .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_3edc0e7b8be5> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read the forces on the atoms." ;
    rdfs:comment "log.forces is a list, one dictionary per atom in the order of the input: {element: [fx, fy, fz]} in Ha/bohr. log.forcemax is the largest component norm." ;
    :hasDescription "Read the forces on the atoms." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "O   [7e-05, -0.01332, -0.0]  |F| = 0.01332 Ha/bohr\nH   [0.00959, 0.00664, 0.0]  |F| = 0.01166 Ha/bohr\nH   [-0.00966, 0.00669, 0.0]  |F| = 0.01175 Ha/bohr\nlargest force: 0.01332 Ha/bohr" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read the forces on the atoms.\n\nlog.forces is a list, one dictionary per atom in the order of the input:\n{element: [fx, fy, fz]} in Ha/bohr. log.forcemax is the largest component norm.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\nnorms = []\nfor atom in log.forces:\n    element, force = list(atom.items())[0]\n    norms.append(float(np.linalg.norm(force)))\n    print(\"%-2s  %s  |F| = %.5f Ha/bohr\" % (element, np.round(force, 5).tolist(), norms[-1]))\n\nassert len(log.forces) == log.nat\nassert abs(max(norms) - log.forcemax) < 1.0e-4\nprint(\"largest force:\", round(log.forcemax, 5), \"Ha/bohr\")\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_47fc2d353eb4> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Build the density of states of a run, as a table and as a figure." ;
    rdfs:comment "log.get_dos() returns a DoS built from the orbital energies, in eV. dump() gives two columns of text (energy, density); plot() draws on a matplotlib axis. Use the Agg backend where there is no display." ;
    :hasDescription "Build the density of states of a run, as a table and as a figure." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "points: 2500 | from -26.4 to -6.3 eV\nwritten: dos.dat, dos.png" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Build the density of states of a run, as a table and as a figure.\n\nlog.get_dos() returns a DoS built from the orbital energies, in eV. dump()\ngives two columns of text (energy, density); plot() draws on a matplotlib\naxis. Use the Agg backend where there is no display.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport matplotlib\n\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\ndos = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\").get_dos(label=\"water\")\n\ntable = dos.dump(sigma=0.2)                              # gaussian broadening, in eV\nrows = [line.split() for line in table.strip().splitlines()]\nassert len(rows) > 100 and len(rows[0]) == 2\nwith open(\"dos.dat\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(table)\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots()\ndos.plot(sigma=0.2, ax=ax)\nfig.savefig(\"dos.png\", dpi=150)\n\nprint(\"points:\", len(rows), \"| from %.1f to %.1f eV\" % (float(rows[0][0]), float(rows[-1][0])))\nprint(\"written: dos.dat, dos.png\")\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_bc671d09a148> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Compare two finished runs: an energy difference, converted, with missing runs handled." ;
    rdfs:comment "Read each log once into a dictionary NAME -> energy, skipping what is not finished, then apply the formula. Total energies are in hartree: 1 Ha = 27.2114 eV = 2625.50 kJ/mol = 627.51 kcal/mol." ;
    :hasDescription "Compare two finished runs: an energy difference, converted, with missing runs handled." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "Found 16 different runs\nrelaxation energy: 0.00136 Ha = 0.0369 eV = 3.56 kJ/mol" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Compare two finished runs: an energy difference, converted, with missing runs handled.\n\nRead each log once into a dictionary NAME -> energy, skipping what is not\nfinished, then apply the formula. Total energies are in hartree:\n1 Ha = 27.2114 eV = 2625.50 kJ/mol = 627.51 kcal/mol.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport os\n\nfrom BigDFT.DoS import AU_eV\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nHA_KJ_MOL = 2625.4996394799\n\n\ndef energy(name, run_dir=\".\"):\n    \"\"\"Final energy of a run, or None if it is not there or did not finish.\"\"\"\n    path = os.path.join(run_dir, \"log-%s.yaml\" % name)\n    if not os.path.isfile(path):\n        return None\n    try:\n        log = Logfile(path)\n        return getattr(log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1], \"energy\", None)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\nE = {name: energy(name) for name in (\"h2o\", \"h2o_relax\", \"not_computed\", \"refused\")}\nassert E[\"not_computed\"] is None and E[\"refused\"] is None        # absent, and refused by BigDFT\ndone = {name: e for name, e in E.items() if e is not None}\n\ngain = done[\"h2o\"] - done[\"h2o_relax\"]\nprint(\"relaxation energy: %.5f Ha = %.4f eV = %.2f kJ/mol\" % (gain, gain * AU_eV, gain * HA_KJ_MOL))\nassert 0 < gain < 0.01\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_relaxation_attributes_are_lowest_energy .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_16dc4c2b2af1> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "After a restart from wavefunctions, check that BigDFT really read them." ;
    rdfs:comment "If the wavefunction files are not where BigDFT looks (data-NAME/), it does not stop: it warns \"Missing wavefunction files, switch to normal input guess\" and starts from scratch. The run succeeds, with the same energy and more iterations. Only the warning tells." ;
    :hasDescription "After a restart from wavefunctions, check that BigDFT really read them." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Chain_calculations ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "pbe0_restart: wavefunctions read, 8 iterations\npbe0_cold   : files missing, started from scratch, 11 iterations" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"After a restart from wavefunctions, check that BigDFT really read them.\n\nIf the wavefunction files are not where BigDFT looks (data-NAME/), it does not\nstop: it warns \"Missing wavefunction files, switch to normal input guess\" and\nstarts from scratch. The run succeeds, with the same energy and more iterations.\nOnly the warning tells.\n\ntask: Chain calculations\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile, find_iterations\n\n\ndef restart_used(path):\n    log = Logfile(path)\n    warnings = [str(w) for w in (log.log.get(\"WARNINGS\") or [])]\n    return not any(\"Missing wavefunction files\" in w for w in warnings)\n\n\ndef iterations(path):\n    return int(sum(len(row) for row in find_iterations(Logfile(path).log)))\n\n\nassert restart_used(\"log-pbe0_restart.yaml\")\nassert not restart_used(\"log-pbe0_cold.yaml\")\nprint(\"pbe0_restart: wavefunctions read,\", iterations(\"log-pbe0_restart.yaml\"), \"iterations\")\nprint(\"pbe0_cold   : files missing, started from scratch,\", iterations(\"log-pbe0_cold.yaml\"), \"iterations\")\nassert iterations(\"log-pbe0_restart.yaml\") < iterations(\"log-pbe0_cold.yaml\")\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_missing_wavefunctions_only_warn .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_4949e483cb32> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Restart a calculation from the wavefunctions of an earlier one." ;
    rdfs:comment "Three steps. The earlier run must have written its orbitals (write_orbitals_on_disk): they are in data-EARLIER/, one file per orbital. The new run reads them from ITS OWN data directory, data-NEW/: copy the wavefunction-* files there. And its input says read_orbitals_from_disk(), which writes dft.inputpsiid = 2. Another functional or another grid spacing is fine." ;
    :hasDescription "Restart a calculation from the wavefunctions of an earlier one." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Chain_calculations ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "copied 5 files to data-h2o_pbe0/ ; input ready: h2o_pbe0.yaml\nsend h2o_pbe0.yaml AND data-h2o_pbe0/ to where it is computed" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Restart a calculation from the wavefunctions of an earlier one.\n\nThree steps. The earlier run must have written its orbitals\n(write_orbitals_on_disk): they are in data-EARLIER/, one file per orbital. The\nnew run reads them from ITS OWN data directory, data-NEW/: copy the\nwavefunction-* files there. And its input says read_orbitals_from_disk(), which\nwrites dft.inputpsiid = 2. Another functional or another grid spacing is fine.\n\ntask: Chain calculations\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nimport glob\nimport os\nimport shutil\n\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\n\n\ndef take_wavefunctions(earlier, new, run_dir=\".\"):\n    \"\"\"Copy the orbitals of the run EARLIER where the run NEW will read them. Returns how many.\"\"\"\n    found = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(run_dir, \"data-\" + earlier, \"wavefunction-*\")))\n    target = os.path.join(run_dir, \"data-\" + new)\n    if found and not os.path.isdir(target):\n        os.makedirs(target)\n    for path in found:\n        shutil.copy2(path, target)\n    return len(found)\n\n\ncopied = take_wavefunctions(\"h2o\", \"h2o_pbe0\")       # h2o is a finished PBE run that wrote its orbitals\nassert copied >= 4, \"the earlier run did not write its orbitals\"\n\ninp = Inputfile()\ninp.set_xc(\"PBE0\")\nfor element in (\"H\", \"O\"):\n    inp[\"psppar.\" + element] = {\"Pseudopotential XC\": 11}\ninp.read_orbitals_from_disk()\nassert inp[\"dft\"][\"inputpsiid\"] == 2\n\nlog = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False).run(\n    name=\"h2o_pbe0\", input=inp, posinp=\"h2o.xyz\")\nassert log.memory_peak is not None, log.log.get(\"Additional Info\")\nprint(\"copied\", copied, \"files to data-h2o_pbe0/ ; input ready: h2o_pbe0.yaml\")\nprint(\"send h2o_pbe0.yaml AND data-h2o_pbe0/ to where it is computed\")\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_inputpsiid ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_hybrid_needs_pseudopotential ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_wavefunctions_are_read_from_own_data_directory .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_a330b04a1611> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Collect the same quantities from many logs into a table." ;
    rdfs:comment "Loop over the log files, keep the finished runs, and print or save rows. pandas is not installed in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image: use plain lists and csv." ;
    :hasDescription "Collect the same quantities from many logs into a table." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "Found 16 different runs\nh2o             3 atoms  h=0.45  E=-17.20985643 Ha   1 evaluation(s)\nh2o_relax       3 atoms  h=0.45  E=-17.21121191 Ha  16 evaluation(s)\noh              2 atoms  h=0.45  E=-16.51883047 Ha   1 evaluation(s)\npbe0_cold       3 atoms  h=0.45  E=-17.20385733 Ha   1 evaluation(s)\npbe0_restart    3 atoms  h=0.45  E=-17.20385733 Ha   1 evaluation(s)" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Collect the same quantities from many logs into a table.\n\nLoop over the log files, keep the finished runs, and print or save rows.\npandas is not installed in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image: use plain lists and csv.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport csv\nimport glob\n\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\ntry:\n    import pandas  # noqa: F401\n    raise AssertionError(\"pandas is installed here: this snippet can use it\")\nexcept ImportError:\n    pass\n\nrows = []\nfor path in sorted(glob.glob(\"log-*.yaml\")):\n    log = Logfile(path)\n    last = log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1]\n    energy = getattr(last, \"energy\", None)\n    if energy is None:\n        continue                                           # a dry run or a refused input\n    name = path[len(\"log-\"):-len(\".yaml\")]\n    rows.append([name, last.nat, last.grid_spacing, \"%.8f\" % energy, max(len(log), 1)])\n\nwith open(\"results.csv\", \"w\") as f:\n    writer = csv.writer(f)\n    writer.writerow([\"run\", \"atoms\", \"hgrid\", \"energy_Ha\", \"force_evaluations\"])\n    writer.writerows(rows)\n\nfor row in rows:\n    print(\"%-14s %2d atoms  h=%.2f  E=%s Ha  %2d evaluation(s)\" % tuple(row))\nassert \"refused\" not in [r[0] for r in rows] and len(rows) >= 4\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_relaxation_attributes_are_lowest_energy ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_pandas_is_not_installed .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_24a1fde40aa8> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Reach what no attribute gives: the log as a dictionary." ;
    rdfs:comment "log.log is the whole YAML document. Useful keys: the input as BigDFT read it (log.log[\"dft\"], ...), the grid, the wall time, the version, the last SCF iteration. For a relaxation, each step has its own: log[i].log." ;
    :hasDescription "Reach what no attribute gives: the log as a dictionary." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "BigDFT version  : 1.9.1\nfunctional read : -101130 (libxc code of PBE)\nbox (angstroem) : [9.0489, 7.6202, 7.6202]\ngrid points     : 23159 coarse, 482 fine\nlast iteration  : 11 | residue 6.98e-05\nwall time       : 2.3 s" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Reach what no attribute gives: the log as a dictionary.\n\nlog.log is the whole YAML document. Useful keys: the input as BigDFT read it\n(log.log[\"dft\"], ...), the grid, the wall time, the version, the last SCF\niteration. For a relaxation, each step has its own: log[i].log.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\ndoc = log.log\n\ngrid = doc[\"Wavefunctions Descriptors, full simulation domain\"]\nprint(\"BigDFT version  :\", doc[\"Version Number\"])\nprint(\"functional read :\", doc[\"dft\"][\"ixc\"], \"(libxc code of PBE)\")\nprint(\"box (angstroem) :\", doc[\"Sizes of the simulation domain\"][\"Angstroem\"])\nprint(\"grid points     :\", grid[\"Coarse resolution grid\"][\"No. of points\"], \"coarse,\",\n      grid[\"Fine resolution grid\"][\"No. of points\"], \"fine\")\nprint(\"last iteration  :\", doc[\"Last Iteration\"][\"iter\"], \"| residue\", doc[\"Last Iteration\"][\"gnrm\"])\nprint(\"wall time       : %.1f s\" % doc[\"Walltime since initialization\"])\n\nassert doc[\"dft\"][\"hgrids\"] == 0.45 and doc[\"Last Iteration\"][\"EKS\"] == log.energy\n" ;
    :setsParameter :Parameter_dft_hgrids .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_e8020e9c619c> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Plot how the SCF converged: the wavefunction residue at each iteration." ;
    rdfs:comment "find_iterations(log.log) returns an array with one row per SCF cycle; each row holds the residue (gnrm) at every iteration of that cycle." ;
    :hasDescription "Plot how the SCF converged: the wavefunction residue at each iteration." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "11 iterations, from 2.7e-01 to 7.0e-05 (criterion 1e-04)" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Plot how the SCF converged: the wavefunction residue at each iteration.\n\nfind_iterations(log.log) returns an array with one row per SCF cycle; each row\nholds the residue (gnrm) at every iteration of that cycle.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nimport matplotlib\n\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile, find_iterations\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\")\nresidues = [float(x) for row in find_iterations(log.log) for x in row]\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots()\nax.semilogy(range(1, len(residues) + 1), residues, marker=\"o\")\nax.axhline(log.gnrm_cv, linestyle=\"--\")                   # the criterion asked\nax.set_xlabel(\"iteration\")\nax.set_ylabel(\"wavefunction residue\")\nfig.savefig(\"scf.png\", dpi=150)\n\nassert residues[0] > residues[-1] and residues[-1] <= log.gnrm_cv\nprint(len(residues), \"iterations, from %.1e to %.1e (criterion %.0e)\" % (residues[0], residues[-1], log.gnrm_cv))\n" .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_b8ba0bca0fcb> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "Read a spin-polarised result: magnetisation and what was asked." ;
    rdfs:comment "log.magnetization is the total magnetisation BigDFT found; log.total_magn_moment and log.spin_polarization repeat the input (dft.mpol, dft.nspin). Compare them when the spin state matters: a run can converge on another state than expected." ;
    :hasDescription "Read a spin-polarised result: magnetisation and what was asked." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Read_a_result ;
    :runsAtStage "analysis" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "asked : nspin = 2 , mpol = 1\nfound : magnetisation = 1.0\nenergy: -16.518830 Ha" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"Read a spin-polarised result: magnetisation and what was asked.\n\nlog.magnetization is the total magnetisation BigDFT found; log.total_magn_moment\nand log.spin_polarization repeat the input (dft.mpol, dft.nspin). Compare them\nwhen the spin state matters: a run can converge on another state than expected.\n\ntask: Read a result\nstage: analysis\n\"\"\"\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nlog = Logfile(\"log-oh.yaml\")\nprint(\"asked : nspin =\", log.spin_polarization, \", mpol =\", log.total_magn_moment)\nprint(\"found : magnetisation =\", log.magnetization)\nprint(\"energy: %.6f Ha\" % log.energy)\n\nassert log.spin_polarization == 2 and abs(log.magnetization - log.total_magn_moment) < 1.0e-6\nassert not hasattr(Logfile(\"log-h2o.yaml\"), \"magnetization\")     # absent without spin polarisation\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_log_attributes_may_be_absent .

<http://bigdft.org/onto#:CodeSnippet:sha256_f12ccdac8f92> a :CodeSnippet ;
    rdfs:label "A study as one script with two verbs: prepare the runs, then analyse the logs." ;
    rdfs:comment "The shape that fits the HAPS: `prepare` writes and dry-runs every input that is not computed yet and returns the names to send; `analyse` reads the logs that came back and applies the formulas. Both can be repeated: finished runs are skipped, missing ones are simply not in the result." ;
    :hasDescription "A study as one script with two verbs: prepare the runs, then analyse the logs." ;
    :demonstrates :Workflow_Send_runs_to_the_HAPS ;
    :runsAtStage "dry-run" ;
    :verifiedWith "PyBigDFT 0.9, BigDFT 1.9.1, Python 3.7.7" ;
    :printsOutput "to send to the HAPS: ['h2o_cation']\nenergies so far: {'h2o': -17.209856, 'oh': -16.51883, 'h2o_cation': None}" ;
    :hasCode "\"\"\"A study as one script with two verbs: prepare the runs, then analyse the logs.\n\nThe shape that fits the HAPS: `prepare` writes and dry-runs every input that\nis not computed yet and returns the names to send; `analyse` reads the logs\nthat came back and applies the formulas. Both can be repeated: finished runs\nare skipped, missing ones are simply not in the result.\n\ntask: Send runs to the HAPS\nstage: dry-run\n\"\"\"\nimport os\n\nfrom BigDFT.Calculators import SystemCalculator\nfrom BigDFT.DoS import AU_eV\nfrom BigDFT.Inputfiles import Inputfile\nfrom BigDFT.Logfiles import Logfile\n\nRUNS = \".\"            # where NAME.yaml is written and log-NAME.yaml comes back\nWATER = {\"units\": \"angstroem\", \"positions\": [\n    {\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [-0.757, 0.5859, 0.0]}]}\nOH = {\"units\": \"angstroem\", \"positions\": [{\"O\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, {\"H\": [0.0, 0.0, 0.97]}]}\n\n\ndef base():\n    inp = Inputfile()\n    inp.set_xc(\"PBE\")\n    inp.set_hgrid(0.45)\n    return inp\n\n\ndef inputs():\n    \"\"\"Every run of the study: name -> (input, structure).\"\"\"\n    runs = {\"h2o\": (base(), WATER)}\n    radical = base()\n    radical.spin_polarize(mpol=1)\n    runs[\"oh\"] = (radical, OH)\n    cation = base()\n    cation.charge(1)\n    cation.spin_polarize(mpol=1)\n    runs[\"h2o_cation\"] = (cation, WATER)\n    return runs\n\n\ndef energy(name):\n    path = os.path.join(RUNS, \"log-%s.yaml\" % name)\n    if not os.path.isfile(path):\n        return None\n    try:\n        log = Logfile(path)\n        return getattr(log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1], \"energy\", None)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n\n\ndef prepare():\n    code = SystemCalculator(omp=\"1\", dry_run=True, verbose=False)\n    ready, refused = [], {}\n    for name, (inp, posinp) in inputs().items():\n        if energy(name) is not None:\n            continue                                   # computed: a dry run would overwrite its log\n        doc = code.run(name=name, input=inp, posinp=posinp, run_dir=RUNS).log\n        problem = doc.get(\"Additional Info\") or doc.get(\"List of error found while parsing input variables\")\n        if problem:\n            refused[name] = problem\n        else:\n            ready.append(name)\n    return ready, refused\n\n\ndef analyse():\n    E = {name: energy(name) for name in inputs()}\n    out = {}\n    if E[\"h2o\"] is not None and E[\"h2o_cation\"] is not None:\n        out[\"ionisation_energy_eV\"] = (E[\"h2o_cation\"] - E[\"h2o\"]) * AU_eV\n    return E, out\n\n\nready, refused = prepare()\nassert ready == [\"h2o_cation\"] and not refused        # h2o and oh are already computed here\nprint(\"to send to the HAPS:\", ready)\n\nE, results = analyse()\nassert E[\"h2o_cation\"] is None and results == {}      # not back yet: no result, no error\nprint(\"energies so far:\", {k: (round(v, 6) if v is not None else None) for k, v in E.items()})\n" ;
    :avoids :Pitfall_dry_run_overwrites_log .

:Pitfall_dry_run_never_raises a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A dry run returns a log and raises nothing, even when BigDFT refused the input" ;
    :hasDescription "A dry run returns a log and raises nothing, even when BigDFT refused the input" ;
    :hasSymptom "SystemCalculator(dry_run=True).run(...) returns a Logfile; the script goes on and sends an input BigDFT cannot read." ;
    :hasCause "PyBigDFT loads whatever log BigDFT wrote. On a refusal that log ends with the key \"Additional Info\", holding the reason." ;
    :hasRemedy "After a dry run, test `\"Additional Info\" in log.log`. If it is there the input is refused and its value is the reason." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner_run ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Logfiles_Logfile .

:Pitfall_dry_run_accepts_input_errors a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "BigDFT goes on after some input errors, such as a value out of range or a method that does not exist" ;
    :hasDescription "BigDFT goes on after some input errors, such as a value out of range or a method that does not exist" ;
    :hasSymptom "The dry run completes and estimates memory although hgrids = 9.0 or geopt.method = \"NOPE\" was given." ;
    :hasCause "These errors are collected in the log under \"List of error found while parsing input variables\" and repeated in WARNINGS; they do not stop BigDFT." ;
    :hasRemedy "Treat that key as a refusal. Do not send a run whose dry-run log has it." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_hgrids ;
    :concerns :Parameter_geopt_method .

:Pitfall_dry_run_overwrites_log a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A dry run replaces the log of a finished calculation of the same name" ;
    :hasDescription "A dry run replaces the log of a finished calculation of the same name" ;
    :hasSymptom "After preparing a study again, energies that had been computed are gone; Logfile has no attribute energy." ;
    :hasCause "A dry run writes log-NAME.yaml like a real run. skip=True does not prevent it when dry_run=True." ;
    :hasRemedy "Before a dry run, check whether log-NAME.yaml already holds an energy, and leave that run alone." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Calculators_SystemCalculator ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner_run .

:Pitfall_memory_estimate_absent_in_linear_scaling a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A dry run in linear scaling prints no memory estimate" ;
    :hasDescription "A dry run in linear scaling prints no memory estimate" ;
    :hasSymptom "log.memory_peak is absent after a dry run with set_linear_scaling(), although the input is valid." ;
    :hasCause "BigDFT only prints \"Estimated Memory Peak (MB)\" for the cubic algorithm." ;
    :hasRemedy "Never use the memory estimate to decide whether an input was accepted. Use the key \"Additional Info\"." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_set_linear_scaling ;
    :concerns :Attribute_Logfile_memory_peak ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_inputpsiid .

:Pitfall_hybrid_needs_pseudopotential a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A hybrid functional is refused unless the pseudopotentials are named" ;
    :hasDescription "A hybrid functional is refused unless the pseudopotentials are named" ;
    :hasSymptom "The pseudopotential parameter file \"psppar.O\" is lacking, and no registered pseudo found for \"O\"" ;
    :hasCause "BigDFT registers pseudopotentials for LDA and PBE, none for PBE0, B3LYP or HF." ;
    :hasRemedy "For every element, inp[\"psppar.\" + element] = {\"Pseudopotential XC\": 11}, which selects the PBE one. BigDFT then warns \"PSP generated with a different XC\", which is expected." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_set_xc ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_ixc .

:Pitfall_relaxation_attributes_are_lowest_energy a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "On a relaxation, log.energy is the lowest energy met, not the final one" ;
    :hasDescription "On a relaxation, log.energy is the lowest energy met, not the final one" ;
    :hasSymptom "The energy read from the log of a geometry optimisation does not match the last step, nor the geometry in final_NAME.yaml." ;
    :hasCause "The log holds one document per force evaluation. The attributes of the Logfile come from the document of lowest energy (log.reference_log)." ;
    :hasRemedy "Take the last document, log[len(log) - 1]. For code that handles both cases, (log if len(log) == 0 else log[len(log) - 1]).energy, since len(log) is 0 for a single point." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Logfiles_Logfile ;
    :concerns :Attribute_Logfile_energy ;
    :concerns :Attribute_Logfile_forcemax ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_optimize_geometry .

:Pitfall_missing_wavefunctions_only_warn a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A restart whose wavefunction files are missing runs anyway, from scratch" ;
    :hasDescription "A restart whose wavefunction files are missing runs anyway, from scratch" ;
    :hasSymptom "The run succeeds with the right energy but takes as many iterations as without restart." ;
    :hasCause "With inputpsiid = 2 and no file in data-NAME/, BigDFT warns \"Missing wavefunction files, switch to normal input guess\" and continues." ;
    :hasRemedy "After the run, look for that sentence in log.log[\"WARNINGS\"]." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_read_orbitals_from_disk ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_inputpsiid .

:Pitfall_wavefunctions_are_read_from_own_data_directory a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A run reads wavefunctions from its own data directory, not from the run that wrote them" ;
    :hasDescription "A run reads wavefunctions from its own data directory, not from the run that wrote them" ;
    :hasSymptom "read_orbitals_from_disk() is set and the earlier run wrote its orbitals, yet the restart is not used." ;
    :hasCause "The run NAME looks in data-NAME/. The earlier run wrote in data-EARLIER/." ;
    :hasRemedy "Copy data-EARLIER/wavefunction-* into data-NAME/ before the run, and send that directory with the input." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_read_orbitals_from_disk ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_write_orbitals_on_disk .

:Pitfall_dataset_names_not_accepted_by_haps a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "The run names a Dataset builds contain ':' and '.'" ;
    :hasDescription "The run names a Dataset builds contain ':' and '.'" ;
    :hasSymptom "A run named \"h:0.5\" is refused by the HAPS, whose names may only hold letters, digits, '_' and '-'." ;
    :hasCause "Dataset derives the name from the id dictionary, as key:value." ;
    :hasRemedy "Name the runs yourself for the HAPS, e.g. \"water_h050\". Keep Dataset for dry runs and local runs." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Datasets_Dataset_append_run .

:Pitfall_input_actions_are_not_in_dir a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "The methods of an Inputfile do not show in dir(Inputfile)" ;
    :hasDescription "The methods of an Inputfile do not show in dir(Inputfile)" ;
    :hasSymptom "Introspection of the class finds only dictionary methods; set_xc and the others seem not to exist." ;
    :hasCause "The functions of BigDFT.InputActions are attached to each Inputfile when it is created." ;
    :hasRemedy "Every public function of BigDFT.InputActions is a method of an Inputfile instance, called without the first argument." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Inputfiles_Inputfile .

:Pitfall_scf_convergence_default_is_a_string a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "set_scf_convergence() without a value writes the word \"default\"" ;
    :hasDescription "set_scf_convergence() without a value writes the word \"default\"" ;
    :hasSymptom "dft.gnrm_cv holds the string \"default\" instead of a number." ;
    :hasCause "The arguments of the action default to the string 'default'." ;
    :hasRemedy "Always give the value, set_scf_convergence(gnrm=1.0e-5)." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_set_scf_convergence ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_gnrm_cv .

:Pitfall_geometry_optimisation_defaults a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "optimize_geometry() defaults to FIRE, 50 steps and forcemax = 0" ;
    :hasDescription "optimize_geometry() defaults to FIRE, 50 steps and forcemax = 0" ;
    :hasSymptom "A relaxation stops on the fluctuation of the forces, or after 50 steps, far from the accuracy wanted." ;
    :hasCause "forcemax = 0 means no criterion on the largest force." ;
    :hasRemedy "Give method, nsteps and forcemax (Ha/bohr) explicitly." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_optimize_geometry ;
    :concerns :Parameter_geopt_forcemax ;
    :concerns :Parameter_geopt_method .

:Pitfall_no_action_for_kpoints a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "No input action sets the k-point mesh in this version" ;
    :hasDescription "No input action sets the k-point mesh in this version" ;
    :hasSymptom "AttributeError: 'Inputfile' object has no attribute 'set_kpt_mesh'" ;
    :hasCause "PyBigDFT 0.9 has no such action; later versions and some tutorials do." ;
    :hasRemedy "Write the keys, inp[\"kpt\"] = {\"method\": \"mpgrid\", \"ngkpt\": [2, 2, 2]}." ;
    :concerns :Parameter_kpt_ngkpt ;
    :concerns :Parameter_kpt_method .

:Pitfall_implicit_solvent_takes_no_solvent_name a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "set_implicit_solvent() takes no solvent name in this version" ;
    :hasDescription "set_implicit_solvent() takes no solvent name in this version" ;
    :hasSymptom "TypeError: set_implicit_solvent() got an unexpected keyword argument 'solvent'" ;
    :hasCause "In PyBigDFT 0.9 its arguments are itermax and minres; it switches on the soft-sphere cavity with the parameters of water." ;
    :hasRemedy "For another solvent write psolver.environment.epsilon and the cavity parameters as keys." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_set_implicit_solvent ;
    :concerns :Parameter_psolver_environment_cavity .

:Pitfall_scipy_cannot_be_imported a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "Functions that import scipy fail in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image" ;
    :hasDescription "Functions that import scipy fail in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image" ;
    :hasSymptom "\"ImportError: libifport.so.5: cannot open shared object file\", for instance from Systems.system_from_log." ;
    :hasCause "scipy.linalg of that image needs a library the image does not carry." ;
    :hasRemedy "Avoid those functions there. For the structure of a run, build the System from log.astruct with system_from_dict_positions." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Systems_system_from_log ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Systems_System_compute_matching .

:Pitfall_readers_take_open_files a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "read_xyz and write_xyz take an open file, not a file name" ;
    :hasDescription "read_xyz and write_xyz take an open file, not a file name" ;
    :hasSymptom "An error on a string, or an empty system." ;
    :hasCause "The readers and writers of BigDFT.IO work on file objects. fragmentation is \"atomic\" or \"single\" and nothing else." ;
    :hasRemedy "with open(name) as ifile: system = read_xyz(ifile)." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_IO_read_xyz ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_IO_write_xyz .

:Pitfall_fragment_geometry_is_in_bohr a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "Fragment.translate and centroid work in bohr" ;
    :hasDescription "Fragment.translate and centroid work in bohr" ;
    :hasSymptom "A molecule moved by \"3\" ends up 1.59 angstroem away." ;
    :hasCause "Positions are stored in bohr whatever units the atoms were given in." ;
    :hasRemedy "Divide a length in angstroem by BigDFT.Atoms.AU_to_A before translating; multiply a centroid or a distance by it to read angstroem." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Fragments_Fragment_translate ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Fragments_Fragment_centroid ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Fragments_distance .

:Pitfall_log_attributes_may_be_absent a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "An attribute of a Logfile exists only if the log holds the quantity" ;
    :hasDescription "An attribute of a Logfile exists only if the log holds the quantity" ;
    :hasSymptom "\"AttributeError: 'Logfile' object has no attribute 'energy'\" (or pressure, magnetization, kpts...)" ;
    :hasCause "Attributes are created from the content of the log; a dry-run log has no energy, an isolated system no pressure." ;
    :hasRemedy "getattr(log, name, None), and treat a missing energy as \"not computed\"." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Logfiles_Logfile .

:Pitfall_orbital_energies_are_padded_with_nan a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "With spin polarisation the shorter list of orbital energies is padded with nan" ;
    :hasDescription "With spin polarisation the shorter list of orbital energies is padded with nan" ;
    :hasSymptom "max() or a sum over log.evals gives nan." ;
    :hasCause "log.evals[k] has one row per spin and as many columns as the larger of the two." ;
    :hasRemedy "Drop the nan of each row before using it, row[~numpy.isnan(row)]." ;
    :concerns :Attribute_Logfile_evals .

:Pitfall_molecule_is_not_a_system a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "Database.Molecules.Molecule is a posinp dictionary, not a System" ;
    :hasDescription "Database.Molecules.Molecule is a posinp dictionary, not a System" ;
    :hasSymptom "AttributeError: 'Molecule' object has no attribute 'get_posinp'" ;
    :hasCause "Molecule(name) already is the dictionary a calculator takes as posinp." ;
    :hasRemedy "Pass it directly as posinp. For a System, system_from_dict_positions(m[\"positions\"], units=m[\"units\"])." ;
    :concerns :Class_BigDFT_Database_Molecules_Molecule ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Systems_system_from_dict_positions .

:Pitfall_structure_file_name_does_not_travel a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "A structure given as a file name is not copied into the input" ;
    :hasDescription "A structure given as a file name is not copied into the input" ;
    :hasSymptom "The input works where it was prepared and fails elsewhere, the .xyz not being found." ;
    :hasCause "With posinp=\"file.xyz\" the input only refers to the file." ;
    :hasRemedy "Give a dictionary, system.get_posinp(), so that NAME.yaml holds the positions." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Calculators_Runner_run ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Systems_System_get_posinp .

:Pitfall_odd_electrons_accepted a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "An odd number of electrons without spin polarisation is accepted" ;
    :hasDescription "An odd number of electrons without spin polarisation is accepted" ;
    :hasSymptom "The calculation runs; only a warning \"Odd number of electrons, no closed shell system\" says something is off." ;
    :hasCause "BigDFT does not refuse the input." ;
    :hasRemedy "Count the electrons when a charge is set; use spin_polarize(mpol=...) with the parity of the electron count, or charge_and_polarize()." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_charge ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_spin_polarize ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_qcharge ;
    :concerns :Parameter_dft_mpol .

:Pitfall_pandas_is_not_installed a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "pandas is not installed in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image" ;
    :hasDescription "pandas is not installed in the BigDFT 1.9.1 image" ;
    :hasSymptom "\"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pandas'\", also from System.to_dataframe." ;
    :hasCause "The image does not carry it." ;
    :hasRemedy "Use lists and the csv module for tables." ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_Systems_System_to_dataframe .

:Pitfall_gpu_acceleration_not_checked_by_dry_run a :Pitfall ;
    rdfs:label "An input asking for a GPU passes the dry run and stops at start where there is none" ;
    :hasDescription "An input asking for a GPU passes the dry run and stops at start where there is none" ;
    :hasSymptom "\"No OpenCL platform available! GPUassert: CUDA driver is a stub library\", exit code 34." ;
    :hasCause "use_gpu_acceleration() writes perf.accel and psolver.setup.accel; a dry run does not try the device." ;
    :hasRemedy "Only call use_gpu_acceleration() for a machine known to have a GPU. (Not asserted by a snippet. Observed: A PBE0 run of water with these two keys, in the CPU image of the pack, on 2026-11-14. The dry run printed a memory estimate; `bigdft -n` exited with code 34.)" ;
    :concerns :Function_BigDFT_InputActions_use_gpu_acceleration ;
    :concerns :Parameter_perf_accel .
